export let frontmatter = {
  "title": "Google Cloud Storage",
  "description": "Back the cache with a GCS bucket: authentication, the resumable-upload chunk size, and the timeout fields whose names disagree with their units."
};
export let structuredData = {
  "contents": [{
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "**Who this is for:** anyone running Forge on Google Cloud who wants the\ndurable tier to be a GCS bucket. &#x2A;*What you'll have at the end:** a\nbucket-backed CAS behind a local fast tier, authenticated by the ambient\nservice account. &#x2A;*Time:** twenty minutes, most of it IAM."
  }, {
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "A config file you can edit (see Configuration), and a GCS bucket you can write to."
  }, {
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "GCS is one `provider` value of the same cloud object store used by\nS3 and compatible,\nAzure Blob and\nOCI Object Storage. The composition\naround it is identical; only the provider block changes."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-recipe",
    "content": "`bucket` is the only field you have to set. No region is needed: a GCS bucket's\nlocation is a property of the bucket, decided when you create it, and the\nclient reaches it the same way wherever it lives. Put the bucket in the region\nyour workers run in; cross-region reads are both slower and billed."
  }, {
    "heading": "authentication",
    "content": "Credentials come from the ambient Google credential chain: a credentials file\nnamed by `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS` (or inline JSON in\n`GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS_JSON`), the application-default credentials\nwritten by `gcloud auth application-default login`, or otherwise the metadata\nserver on GCE, GKE or Cloud Run. Nothing secret goes in the config file."
  }, {
    "heading": "authentication",
    "content": "The service account needs to read and write objects in the bucket;\n`roles/storage.objectUser` scoped to the bucket covers it (overwriting an\nexisting object in GCS also needs the delete permission that role includes).\nForge itself never deletes objects; expiry is a bucket lifecycle rule."
  }, {
    "heading": "authentication",
    "content": "`authentication_required` defaults to `false`: if no credential is found, the\nstore starts anyway and issues anonymous requests to `storage.googleapis.com`\n(there is no endpoint override for an emulator). Set it to `true` for anything real,\nso a misconfigured credential chain fails loudly at startup rather than as a\npermission error on the first request."
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "Field"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "Default"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "What it decides"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "`key_prefix`"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "none"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "Namespacing inside one bucket; give the CAS `cas/` and the AC `ac/`"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "`resumable_chunk_size`"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "2 MB"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "Chunk size for resumable uploads of large objects; can only be lowered"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "`authentication_required`"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "`false`"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "Whether to error at startup when no credential is found"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "`retry`"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "Exponential backoff with jitter, shared with every other provider"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "`consider_expired_after_s`"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "`0` (never)"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "How old an object may be and still count as present"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "Objects under 5 MB with a known size go up in one request; everything else\nuses a resumable upload, sent chunk by chunk with `resumable_chunk_size`\nbytes per request. The value is rounded to a multiple of 256 KiB and capped at\nthe 2 MB default, so it can only be lowered, which trades more round trips per\nobject for less memory held per in-flight upload. No setting\nraises it."
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "`connection_timeout_s` and `read_timeout_s` carry a documented default of\n`3000` and the words \"in milliseconds\" in the reference. The code reads\nboth as seconds and uses 3 seconds when they are unset. If you set them,\nset them in seconds, and leave them unset unless you are actively debugging\na timeout."
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "The remaining shared options behave as described in\nthe shared options section, with one\ndifference: here `multipart_max_concurrent_uploads` (default 10) caps how many\nrequests this store has in flight to GCS at once, across all operations, and\nthe chunks of one resumable upload are sent one after another.\n`max_retry_buffer_per_request` is raised to at least the chunk size, and\n`insecure_allow_http` and `disable_http2` are not consulted by the GCS\nclient."
  }, {
    "heading": "steps",
    "content": "**Create the bucket** in the region your workers run in. Uniform bucket-level\naccess is fine and simpler than per-object ACLs."
  }, {
    "heading": "steps",
    "content": "**Grant the service account** object read and write on that bucket, and\nnothing wider."
  }, {
    "heading": "steps",
    "content": "**Set `authentication_required: true`** so a missing credential fails at\nstartup. A resumable upload session that a killed process leaves behind\nexpires on its own after a week; there is nothing to clean up."
  }, {
    "heading": "steps",
    "content": "**Add the store** as the `slow` half of a `fast_slow` pair whose `fast` half is\na local filesystem store."
  }, {
    "heading": "steps",
    "content": "**Run a build twice** (once cold, once after emptying the local fast tier)\nand watch object counts in the bucket."
  }, {
    "heading": "steps",
    "content": "Objects appear under `key_prefix` in the bucket during the first build."
  }, {
    "heading": "steps",
    "content": "The second build is a cache hit even after `content_path` is emptied, which\nproves reads fall through to the bucket."
  }, {
    "heading": "steps",
    "content": "Bucket request counts are far lower than blob counts, which proves the fast\ntier is absorbing repeat reads."
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-doesnt-work",
    "content": "The credential chain found something, but it can't act on the bucket. Confirm\nthe service account attached to the instance or workload identity has object\nread and write on it. If it can create but not overwrite, re-uploads of a\ndigest that already exists fail, because GCS needs the delete permission to\nreplace an object."
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-doesnt-work",
    "content": "That's `authentication_required` at its default of `false`. Set it to `true`\nso the store errors at startup instead of quietly issuing unauthenticated\nrequests."
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-doesnt-work",
    "content": "The chunk size is at most 2 MB and each chunk is a round trip, so a large\nobject is many sequential requests; `resumable_chunk_size` can only make the\nchunks smaller. Memory per in-flight upload is bounded by the chunk size plus\nthe retry buffer; the number of concurrent requests is bounded by\n`multipart_max_concurrent_uploads`."
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-doesnt-work",
    "content": "You're reaching the bucket on every read. Confirm the store is the `slow` half\nof a `fast_slow` pair, and that the `fast` half's `eviction_policy` isn't so\nsmall that everything is evicted before it's re-read."
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-doesnt-work",
    "content": "Check `consider_expired_after_s`. A non-zero value makes objects older than\nthat window invisible on purpose, so they pair with a matching bucket lifecycle\nrule. If you didn't intend that, set it back to `0`."
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-doesnt-work",
    "content": "Deduplication, compression and existence caching in front of the bucket,\nthe layers that decide what it actually costs."
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-doesnt-work",
    "content": "The same store type with a different provider, and the shared options in\nfull."
  }],
  "headings": [{
    "id": "the-recipe",
    "content": "The recipe"
  }, {
    "id": "authentication",
    "content": "Authentication"
  }, {
    "id": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "Options worth setting"
  }, {
    "id": "steps",
    "content": "Steps"
  }, {
    "id": "when-it-doesnt-work",
    "content": "When it doesn't work"
  }]
};
