  }, {
    "heading": "what-ships-and-what-this-page-supplies",
    "content": "The default pipeline puts up to two and a half minutes between a queue spike\nand an HPA that can see it. Most of that is fixable, and none of it is\ndocumented anywhere else. It is the next section, and it is the single thing\nmost likely to make a correct-looking autoscaler behave badly."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-reaction-time-budget",
    "content": "The signal an autoscaler reads is not emitted by Forge. It is derived,\nseveral hops downstream, and each hop adds staleness. Here is the whole chain\nwith its shipped defaults."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-reaction-time-budget",
    "content": "Worst case, an action that queues right after an export window closes is\ninvisible to the HPA for about two and a half minutes. Then the HPA's own\nstabilization window applies on top."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-reaction-time-budget",
    "content": "Three of those five hops are yours to fix and two are not worth fixing."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-reaction-time-budget",
    "content": "**The export interval is the big one, and it is an environment variable.** The\nbinary builds its meter provider with a periodic exporter and never sets an\ninterval, so it takes the OpenTelemetry SDK default of 60 seconds. Set\n`OTEL_METRIC_EXPORT_INTERVAL` on the scheduler pod to bring it down."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-reaction-time-budget",
    "content": "**The recording-rule interval is the second.** `forge:queue_depth` lives in\nthe `forge_performance` group in\n`deployment-examples/metrics/prometheus-recording-rules.yml`, and that group is\ndeclared `interval: 60s`. The execution group next to it uses 30s. Either move\nthe rule into a group with a short interval, or skip the recording rule for\nscaling and point the adapter at the raw series."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-reaction-time-budget",
    "content": "**The collector batch timeout** is 10 seconds in the shipped collector config\nand is not worth chasing; it overlaps the scrape interval anyway."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-reaction-time-budget",
    "content": "Every export is a full OTLP push of every instrument. At 5 seconds you are\nmultiplying collector ingest and Prometheus sample volume by twelve for a\nsignal you are going to smooth with a stabilization window regardless. Fifteen\nseconds is a good default and the point of diminishing returns for most pools."
  }, {
    "heading": "five-gaps-you-close-first",
    "content": "The shipped Kubernetes manifests cannot support an HPA as they stand. Not\nbecause of anything subtle, but because of five specific absences. Each one is a\nshort fix and all five are prerequisites."
