    "heading": "what-these-docs-guarantee-to-a-machine-reader",
    "content": "Each of these is enforced by something in the repository, not by an author\nremembering. Where it is a script, the script is named."
  }, {
    "heading": "what-these-docs-guarantee-to-a-machine-reader",
    "content": "**One canonical page per concept.** If two pages would explain the same\nthing, one of them links the other. An agent that finds an answer has found\n*the* answer."
  }, {
    "heading": "what-these-docs-guarantee-to-a-machine-reader",
    "content": "**Stable anchors.** Every heading and every FAQ entry carries an explicit\n`[#anchor]` or `id`, so a citation to a specific claim keeps resolving after\nthe prose around it is reworded."
  }, {
    "heading": "what-these-docs-guarantee-to-a-machine-reader",
    "content": "fails the check if one is missing, and its `--fix` writes the anchor Fumadocs\nwould have derived from the heading text anyway, so pinning an anchor never\nmoves a link that already worked."
  }, {
    "heading": "what-these-docs-guarantee-to-a-machine-reader",
    "content": "**Redirects on every moved URL.** This site's structure changed\nsubstantially; agents hold cached URLs longer than humans hold bookmarks, so\nold paths redirect rather than 404. They live in\n. Follow redirects rather\nthan treating a 301 as a failure."
  }, {
    "heading": "what-these-docs-guarantee-to-a-machine-reader",
    "content": "**Doc-to-source permalinks.** Behavioural claims carry a link to the code\nthat implements them, pinned to a release tag rather than to `main`. A\npermalink that drifts is worse than no link, because the reader can't tell.\nThe pinned ref is a single constant in\n."
  }, {
    "heading": "what-these-docs-guarantee-to-a-machine-reader",
    "content": "**Generated reference.** The configuration reference, the metrics reference\nand the changelog are generated from the source of truth in the repo rather\nthan transcribed from it. An agent reading the docs and an agent reading the\ncode get the same answer by construction. Config snippets in narrative pages\nare checked against that generated reference by\n, so a snippet\ncannot quietly reference a field that no longer exists."
  }, {
    "heading": "what-these-docs-guarantee-to-a-machine-reader",
    "content": "**Every internal link resolves, and every page on the path has a next step.**\n and\n run on every\nchange, so a crawl never hits a dead internal link or a dead end."
  }, {
    "heading": "what-these-docs-guarantee-to-a-machine-reader",
    "content": "**Machine-detectable structure.** Verification blocks carry\n`data-verify-block`; prerequisite blocks carry `data-prerequisites`; next\nsteps carry `data-next-step`; version badges carry `data-min-version`; source\nlinks carry `data-source-link` and `data-source-ref`. Ordering and\nprovability are readable without parsing prose."
  }, {
    "heading": "what-is-not-guaranteed",
    "content": "Being specific about the edges is more useful than a blanket claim."
  }, {
    "heading": "what-is-not-guaranteed",
    "content": "**Prose is not generated.** Everything outside the generated reference is\nwritten by a human and checked against the source at the pinned release, not\nby a script. A behavioural claim carrying a `<SourceLink>` has been checked\nagainst that file at the pinned tag; a claim without one has not been\nmechanically checked against anything."
  }, {
    "heading": "what-is-not-guaranteed",
    "content": "**The pinned ref lags releases.** `<SourceLink>` targets a release tag, so\nimmediately after a release lands the links point at the previous one until\nthe reference is regenerated. That is the deliberate trade: a stale-but-honest\npermalink over a `main` link that silently means something different next\nweek."
  }, {
    "heading": "what-is-not-guaranteed",
    "content": "**Third-party tools are described from their own documentation.** Bazel,\nBuck2, Siso, Pants, BuildStream and recc flags are taken from those projects'\ndocs at the time of writing; Forge's source cannot vouch for them."
  }, {
    "heading": "what-is-not-guaranteed",
    "content": "If you're here to actually run Forge rather than to point something\nelse at it, Getting started is the start of the reading path."
  }],
