    "content": "**Get the shape right.** The production configuration is not the quickstart\nconfiguration with bigger numbers. It has a fast tier over a durable one,\neviction policies that match your disk, and a deliberate split between the\npublic listeners and the worker API."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-arc",
    "content": "**Deploy it somewhere real.** Docker Compose or bare metal, each with the\ntopology, the resource sizing, and the failure domains that go with it. For\nKubernetes, the Helm charts ship with Forge Enterprise."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-arc",
    "content": "**See it.** OTLP to Prometheus to Grafana, and the specific metrics worth\nalerting on rather than all of them."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-arc",
    "content": "**Scale it.** Workers scale on queue depth and action duration; the CAS\nscales on throughput and eviction pressure. They are separate problems with\nseparate signals, and conflating them is the most common scaling mistake."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-arc",
    "content": "**Tune it.** A small number of levers move the needle. Most of the config\nsurface does not, and knowing which is which saves a lot of afternoons."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-arc",
    "content": "**Harden it.** Port exposure, mTLS, and keeping the worker API private,\nwhich matters more than it sounds, because a worker API is an arbitrary code\nexecution endpoint by design."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-arc",
    "content": "**Have runbooks.** Redis failover, worker OOM, disk full, backpressure. Each\none written down before it happens."
  }, {
    "heading": "start-here-or-skip-ahead",
    "content": "**Start here** if you're moving from a working setup to one people depend on."
