  }, {
    "heading": "current-pages",
    "content": "Observability: the OTLP to Prometheus to\nGrafana pipeline, and why skipping the collector silently breaks every\nshipped dashboard."
  }, {
    "heading": "current-pages",
    "content": "Security hardening: there is no inbound\nauthentication anywhere, so the network is the authorization layer."
  }, {
    "heading": "current-pages",
    "content": "Scaling workers: sizing one worker, the\nqueue-depth signal, and wiring an autoscaler to it."
  }, {
    "heading": "current-pages",
    "content": "Scaling the CAS: composing the store graph, sizing\neviction, and what a second CAS process actually costs."
  }, {
    "heading": "current-pages",
    "content": "An autoscaling reference deployment: the\nmanifests that make the worker pool size itself, and the five gaps in the\nshipped examples you close first."
  }, {
    "heading": "current-pages",
    "content": "Runbooks: the four incidents Forge actually\nproduces: a worker OOM-killed, the disk full, Redis failing over, and a\nqueue that backpressures and never recovers."
  }, {
    "heading": "current-pages",
    "content": "Troubleshooting: symptom to cause to fix,\nindexed on the error strings the system really emits."
