  }, {
    "heading": "style",
    "content": "Vale (`.vale.ini`, error level only) runs over the MDX in pre-commit and in\nthe `Vale` CI check; `typos` excludes `web/`. The house rules on top of that\nare short:"
  }, {
    "heading": "style",
    "content": "**Write prose, not bullet fragments.** A bulleted list of six three-word\nitems is a table that has not admitted it yet. Use a real table, or write\nsentences."
  }, {
    "heading": "style",
    "content": "**One idea per paragraph**, and lead with the claim rather than building up\nto it."
  }, {
    "heading": "style",
    "content": "**Every code block gets a language tag.** Markdown needs it for\nhighlighting, and the snippet lint needs it to find the fence."
  }, {
    "heading": "style",
    "content": "**No em-dashes or en-dashes.** Use a comma, a colon, parentheses, or two\nsentences instead."
  }, {
    "heading": "style",
    "content": "**Say the surprising thing plainly.** If a default is wrong for most people,\nif a name points at the wrong crate, if a policy does not exist, write that\ndown. A page that reads as a brochure is a page that stops being consulted."
  }, {
    "heading": "style",
    "content": "**Link the canonical page rather than restating it.** Field-level truth lives\nin the generated reference; a reading-path page states intent and tradeoffs\nand links out for the types and defaults."
