    }), "\n", _jsxs(_components.p, {
      children: ["Three bounds keep one action from taking the worker with it.\n", _jsx(_components.strong, {
        children: _jsx(_components.code, {
          children: "max_captured_output_bytes"
        })
      }), " (default 0, unbounded) caps how much of an\naction's stdout or stderr the worker holds in memory; past it the output\nspills to a file under the action directory and is uploaded from disk, so a\ntool that prints gigabytes costs disk, not RAM. ", _jsx(_components.strong, {
        children: _jsx(_components.code, {
          children: "precondition_timeout_ms"
        })
      }), "\n(default 30000) ends a hanging precondition script and refuses the action as\nbackpressure. ", _jsx(_components.strong, {
        children: _jsx(_components.code, {
          children: "orphan_sweep_interval_s"
        })
      }), " (default 0, off) removes action\ndirectories under ", _jsx(_components.code, {
        children: "work_directory"
      }), " that no running action owns and that a\nfailed cleanup left behind; the directory is always purged at startup."]
    }), "\n", _jsxs(_components.p, {
      children: ["When the worker ends an action, for a timeout or a scheduler cancel, the\nprocess group gets SIGTERM first and ", _jsx(_components.strong, {
        children: _jsx(_components.code, {
          children: "kill_grace_ms"
        })
      }), " (default 5000) to\nwrite its own cleanup before SIGKILL follows; the memory reservation kill\nskips the grace. A killed action keeps the stdout and stderr it produced.\n", _jsx(_components.strong, {
        children: _jsx(_components.code, {
          children: "set_tmpdir"
        })
      }), " (default true) gives every action its own ", _jsx(_components.code, {
        children: "TMPDIR"
      }), " under its\naction directory, so concurrent actions writing the same temporary file name\nno longer collide; a ", _jsx(_components.code, {
