        children: "/tmp"
      }), " is unaffected. A timeout above ", _jsx(_components.code, {
        children: "max_action_timeout_s"
      }), "\nis clamped to it rather than rejected."]
    }), "\n", _jsxs(_components.p, {
      children: ["When the action's own process has exited, anything it left running in its\nprocess group (a background job, a helper that daemonized) is killed, since\nit would otherwise hold the action's output pipes open and the action would\nsit there until its timeout; the pipes then get five seconds to drain, and\nwhat was read by then is kept. The worker also makes itself the parent of\nevery process an action leaves behind and reaps them on a timer, so a build\nwhose actions fork and do not wait no longer leaves hundreds of zombies on\nthe worker for the life of the pod. Under ", _jsx(_components.code, {
        children: "use_namespaces"
      }), " the stub does\nthe reaping inside the action's PID namespace."]
    }), "\n", _jsxs(_components.p, {
      children: ["Every executed action reports its resource usage to the scheduler with an\n", _jsx(_components.code, {
        children: "outcome"
