export let structuredData = {
  "contents": [{
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "**Who this is for:** anyone who already operates MongoDB. &#x2A;*What you'll have\nat the end:** a Mongo-backed CAS behind a local fast tier. &#x2A;*Time:**\ntwenty-five minutes."
  }, {
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "A config file you can edit (see Configuration), and a reachable MongoDB deployment."
  }, {
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "Mongo lands between Redis and\nobject storage: durable, shared across\nmachines, single-digit milliseconds away, and priced by the cluster you run\nrather than per gigabyte stored. Storage backends compares\nall of them on the same axes."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-recipe",
    "content": "`connection_string` is the only required field and takes either form Mongo\naccepts, `mongodb://localhost:27017` or\n`mongodb+srv://cluster.mongodb.net` for Atlas. It carries the credentials, so\nkeep it in the environment and reference it with `${VAR}`; see\nThe config file."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-recipe",
    "content": "Everything else has a default: `database` is `forge`, `cas_collection` is\n`cas`, `scheduler_collection` is `scheduler`, and `key_prefix` is empty."
  }, {
    "heading": "change-streams-and-the-scheduler",
    "content": "The Mongo store implements the scheduler-store interface, and\n`enable_change_streams: true` is what that interface needs: the store refuses\nto hand out scheduler subscriptions without it. In v1.6.5, though, the `simple`\nscheduler's `experimental_backend` accepts only `memory` and `redis`, so there\nis no config path that puts a Mongo store behind the scheduler. Treat this\nstore as a CAS and Action Cache backend, and see\nRedis for a shared scheduler."
  }, {
    "heading": "change-streams-and-the-scheduler",
    "content": "Leave `enable_change_streams` off for a store used as a CAS. It buys nothing\nthere."
  }, {
    "heading": "change-streams-and-the-scheduler",
    "content": "Mongo only offers change streams on a replica set or sharded cluster; a\nstandalone `mongod` cannot serve them, no matter what this flag says. Atlas\nis always a replica set; a local single-node deployment needs\n`--replSet` and an initiated set."
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "Field"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "Default"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "What it decides"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "`database`"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "`forge`"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "Database name"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "`cas_collection`"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "`cas`"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "Collection holding CAS objects"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "`scheduler_collection`"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "`scheduler`"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "Collection holding scheduler state"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "`key_prefix`"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "empty"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "Namespacing when several deployments share one database"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "`read_chunk_size`"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "64 KB"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "Bytes pulled per chunk when streaming a blob out"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "`max_requests`"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "unlimited"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "Ceiling on concurrent requests to the deployment"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "`connection_timeout_ms`"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "3000"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "Applied as both the driver's connect timeout and its server-selection timeout"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "`command_timeout_ms`"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "10000"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "Accepted and defaulted, but not applied to any driver option in v1.6.5"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "`enable_change_streams`"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "`false`"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "Required for scheduler subscriptions, which nothing uses yet (see above)"
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "Write concern is exposed as three separate fields mirroring Mongo's own:\n`write_concern_w` (a number like `1`, or the string `\"majority\"`),\n`write_concern_j` (whether to wait for the journal), and\n`write_concern_timeout_ms`. All three are optional and unset means the\ndeployment's own default applies, but `write_concern_j` or\n`write_concern_timeout_ms` without `write_concern_w` is rejected at startup.\nFor a CAS, `\"majority\"` is the honest\nsetting, because a cache entry acknowledged by one node and then lost to a failover is\na cache entry a client believes exists."
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "`max_requests` is the equivalent of Redis's permit ceiling and is unlimited by\ndefault. Set it if bursts are overwhelming the deployment; queuing in\nForge beats timing out at Mongo. Zero is rejected at startup."
  }, {
    "heading": "options-worth-setting",
    "content": "It survives in the schema for compatibility. Setting it only logs a warning;\nuse `max_requests` to bound concurrency."
  }, {
    "heading": "steps",
    "content": "**Provision the deployment**: a replica set if you want writes to survive a\nfailover with `\"majority\"` write concern."
  }, {
    "heading": "steps",
    "content": "**Create an architect** with read and write on the database, and put the full\nconnection string in the environment rather than the config file."
  }, {
    "heading": "steps",
    "content": "**Add the store**, choosing a `key_prefix` if this database is shared with\nanother Forge deployment."
  }, {
    "heading": "steps",
    "content": "**Set write concern** to `\"majority\"` for anything you intend to trust."
  }, {
    "heading": "steps",
    "content": "**Run a build twice**, the second time from a different machine, to confirm the\nstore is genuinely shared."
  }, {
    "heading": "steps",
    "content": "Documents appear in the CAS collection during the first build."
  }, {
    "heading": "steps",
    "content": "A second machine pointed at the same deployment gets cache hits for objects\nthe first one uploaded."
  }, {
    "heading": "steps",
    "content": "No connection or server-selection timeouts in the logs at your normal peak\nload."
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-doesnt-work",
    "content": "Not in v1.6.5. The store implements the scheduler-store interface behind\n`enable_change_streams`, but the `simple` scheduler's `experimental_backend`\nonly accepts `memory` and `redis`, so there is nothing to point at it. Use\nRedis for a shared scheduler."
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-doesnt-work",
    "content": "Use the `mongodb+srv://` form, and check that the deployment's IP access list\nincludes wherever Forge runs. An access-list rejection often surfaces as a\nconnection timeout rather than as an authorization error."
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-doesnt-work",
    "content": "Set `max_requests` so concurrency queues in Forge instead of arriving all\nat once, then consider raising `connection_timeout_ms`, which also bounds\nserver selection. Also check the deployment's own connection limit; Atlas\ntiers cap it low."
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-doesnt-work",
    "content": "Write concern. With `write_concern_w` unset or `1`, a write acknowledged by the\nprimary can be rolled back when that primary is replaced. Set `\"majority\"`."
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-doesnt-work",
    "content": "They share a database with no `key_prefix`, or the same one. Give each its own\nprefix, or its own database."
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-doesnt-work",
    "content": "Putting a local fast tier in front of this one, and the rest of the\ncomposition vocabulary."
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-doesnt-work",
    "content": "The backend that can hold scheduler state in v1.6.5, if you need several\nschedulers to share one queue."
  }],
  "headings": [{
