  }, {
    "heading": "troubleshooting",
    "content": "**Buck2 cannot connect.** Confirm Forge is listening on `50051` and\nBuck2 is not expecting TLS."
  }, {
    "heading": "troubleshooting",
    "content": "**Everything runs locally.** Check that your selected execution platform\nsets `remote_enabled = True`."
  }, {
    "heading": "troubleshooting",
    "content": "**Instance-name errors.** Make sure Buck2's `instance_name` matches the\nForge config. The integration test uses `main`."
  }, {
    "heading": "faq",
    "content": "`engine_address`, `action_cache_address`, and `cas_address` are\nseparate settings because Buck2 lets you split those services across\nhosts. Forge serves them all from one listener, so all three\npoint at the same `host:port`."
  }, {
    "heading": "faq",
    "content": "Both. Execution needs an execution platform registered with\n`remote_enabled = True` (above) plus a Forge scheduler and\nworker; the integration test config runs one of each."
  }, {
    "heading": "faq",
