import {Fragment as _Fragment, jsx as _jsx, jsxs as _jsxs} from "react/jsx-runtime";
export let frontmatter = {
  "title": "How to extend Forge",
  "description": "Complete file-by-file recipes for adding a store, a config field, a metric, or a gRPC service."
};
export let structuredData = {
  "contents": [{
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "**Who this is for:** anyone adding a new component rather than changing an\nexisting one. &#x2A;*What you'll have at the end:** four recipes, each listing\nevery file a working change touches, including the ones that compile fine\nwhen you forget them and fail in CI. &#x2A;*Time:** use as a checklist."
  }, {
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "Each recipe below is derived from the smallest existing example in the tree.\nCopy that example rather than starting from a blank file: it already has the\nright license header, the right derives, and the right last line."
  }, {
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "Read codebase internals first if you have\nnot; the trait split and the spawning rules are assumed here."
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-store",
    "content": "Model: `forge-store/src/noop_store.rs`, the smallest complete\n`StoreDriver` in the tree."
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-store",
    "content": "**Add the spec** to `forge-config/src/stores.rs`. A new variant on\n`StoreSpec` (the JSON5 key is the snake\\_case form of the variant name;\nbox the payload if it is large) plus a spec struct modelled on\n`MemorySpec`:"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-store",
    "content": "The `dev-schema` `cfg_attr` is not optional; without it your store never\nappears in the generated\nconfiguration reference."
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-store",
    "content": "**Write the store** at `forge-store/src/my_store.rs`: the license\nheader copied from a neighbouring file, the struct, a `MetricsComponent`\nimpl, `pub fn new(...) -> Arc<Self>`, `#[async_trait] impl StoreDriver`,\nand `default_health_status_indicator!(MyStore);` as the last line."
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-store",
    "content": "**Declare the module**: `pub mod my_store;` in\n`forge-store/src/lib.rs`."
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-store",
    "content": "**Wire the factory**: an import and a match arm in\n`forge-store/src/default_store_factory.rs`. The match is exhaustive,\nso this one is a compile error if you forget it. It is the only step that\nis."
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-store",
    "content": "**Add the file to `forge-store/BUILD.bazel`**, in the `srcs` list,\n**alphabetically**. Cargo does not care. Bazel does, and CI runs Bazel;\nthis is the single most common way a store PR goes red after a green\nlocal run."
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-store",
    "content": "**Add a test** at `forge-store/tests/my_store_test.rs` and register\nit in the crate's `rust_test_suite`. See\nthe testing guide."
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-store",
    "content": "`forge-config/examples/stores-config.json5` is produced by the\n`generate-stores-config` tool from the ` ```json ` fenced blocks in\nthe doc comments in `stores.rs`, via a pre-commit hook. And\n`tests/json5_test.rs` parses every example, so a malformed JSON fence in a\ndoc comment is not a cosmetic problem; it breaks the build."
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-store",
    "content": "Two semantics to get right, both covered in\nthe store model:"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-store",
    "content": "**`inner_store` must return `self`** if your store changes the bytes on the\nway through, and forward to the inner store if it only routes. Returning the\nwrong one is a runtime error, not a compile error."
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-store",
    "content": "**`update` must drain its reader** even when it is discarding the data.\n`NoopStore` does this; a store that returns early without draining will hang\nits writer."
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-config-field",
    "content": "Config fields are documentation. The doc comment becomes the description in\nthe generated reference, and the ` ```json ` fences in `stores.rs` are\nalso harvested into the examples file, which is why they have to be valid\nJSON rather than illustrative fragments."
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-config-field",
    "content": "**Add the field with a doc comment ending in a default line:**"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-config-field",
    "content": "The `Default:` line is parsed out of the description by the docs\ngenerator. Without it the reference shows no default."
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-config-field",
    "content": "**Pick the right `deserialize_with` helper** from\n.\nThey all expand shell variables, which is how a config file references\nthe environment."
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-config-field",
    "content": "**Regenerate the reference** if you want to see the result:\n`bun --filter @forge/docs gen:config-reference` from `web/`."
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-config-field",
    "content": "The helpers that exist:"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-config-field",
    "content": "Helper"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-config-field",
    "content": "For"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-config-field",
    "content": "`convert_numeric_with_shellexpand`"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-config-field",
    "content": "Any integer type"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-config-field",
    "content": "`convert_optional_numeric_with_shellexpand`"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-config-field",
    "content": "`Option<N>`"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-config-field",
    "content": "`convert_string_with_shellexpand`"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-config-field",
    "content": "`String`"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-config-field",
    "content": "`convert_optional_string_with_shellexpand`"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-config-field",
    "content": "`Option<String>`"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-config-field",
    "content": "`convert_vec_string_with_shellexpand`"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-config-field",
    "content": "`Vec<String>`"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-config-field",
    "content": "`convert_boolean_with_shellexpand`"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-config-field",
    "content": "`bool`"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-config-field",
    "content": "`convert_data_size_with_shellexpand`"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-config-field",
    "content": "Byte sizes; accepts `1GB`, `512MiB`"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-config-field",
    "content": "`convert_optional_data_size_with_shellexpand`"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-config-field",
    "content": "`Option<size>`"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-config-field",
    "content": "`convert_duration_with_shellexpand`"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-config-field",
    "content": "Durations"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-config-field",
    "content": "`convert_duration_with_shellexpand_and_negative`"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-config-field",
    "content": "Durations that may be negative"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-config-field",
    "content": "A `bool` that should default to `true` needs its own\n`fn default_true() -> bool { true }` and `#[serde(default = \"default_true\")]`.\nSeveral fields do this; there is no shared helper."
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-config-field",
    "content": "To rename a field without breaking existing configs, add a shim in\n`backcompat.rs`; both existing shims are `#[serde(untagged)]` enums that\naccept the old and new shapes and emit a `tracing::warn!` on the deprecated\none."
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-metric",
    "content": "Decide which system first; see\ntwo metric systems."
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-metric",
    "content": "**The derive path** touches one file. Add the field, annotate it:"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-metric",
    "content": "The struct already derives `MetricsComponent`, and the value appears in the\nintrospection tree automatically."
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-metric",
    "content": "**The OpenTelemetry path** touches three:"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-metric",
    "content": "Declare the instrument in the appropriate `LazyLock` bundle in\n`forge-util/src/metrics.rs` (`CACHE_METRICS`, `EXECUTION_METRICS`,\n`WORKER_METRICS`, `RPC_METRICS`, `SCHEDULER_METRICS`,\n`STORE_TIER_METRICS`, `HEALTH_METRICS` or `CONNECTION_METRICS`). Use a\ndotted name, a `.with_description`, and a `.with_unit` that is a UCUM\nunit (`\"By\"`, `\"s\"`, `\"ms\"`) or a braced count such as `\"{entry}\"`.\nThen regenerate the metrics reference with\n`bun --filter @forge/docs gen:metrics-reference` from `web/`, which\nreads this file."
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-metric",
    "content": "Record it at the call site, using the pre-computed attribute struct\nwhere one exists (`CacheMetricAttrs` / `ExecutionMetricAttrs`) rather\nthan building attributes inline."
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-metric",
    "content": "Extend `forge-util/tests/metrics_test.rs`."
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-metric",
    "content": "`forge-util/src/metrics.rs` is **Business Source License**; keep its\nheader, do not paste the FSL one in. And never add an action digest or a\nworker ID as an attribute on a hot instrument: the cardinality will kill\nthe metrics backend long before it affects Forge."
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-grpc-service",
    "content": "Model: `forge-service/src/fetch_server.rs`: 165 lines, and it has\nevery convention in it."
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-grpc-service",
    "content": "**Write the server** at `forge-service/src/my_server.rs`. Import\nthe generated trait and server type with the standard alias:"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-grpc-service",
    "content": "Hold per-instance state in a `HashMap<String, _>` keyed by instance\nname. Constructor signature:"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-grpc-service",
    "content": "**Provide `into_service`**, exactly this name, because the\n`service_setup!` macro calls it:"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-grpc-service",
    "content": "**Split each RPC in two.** A private `inner_<rpc>` returning\n`forge_error::Error` holds the logic; the public\n`#[tonic::async_trait]` method wraps it, converts to `Status`, and\ncarries the instrumentation:"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-grpc-service",
    "content": "**Register it** in the `Routes::builder().routes()` chain in\n`src/bin/forge.rs`, with `.add_optional_service(...)` and\n`service_setup!`. The macro applies the message-size limit (4 MiB by\ndefault) and compression settings, so registering without it silently\nopts out of both."
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-grpc-service",
    "content": "If the service needs new protos: add the package to `PROTO_NAMES` **and** to\nthe `gen_rs_protos` `srcs` list in `forge-proto/BUILD.bazel`, then\nregenerate and commit the output:"
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-grpc-service",
    "content": "`//forge-proto:update_protos_test` is the CI gate that catches a\nforgotten regeneration."
  }, {
    "heading": "adding-a-grpc-service",
    "content": "The CAS server carries an explicit note about this: the `worker_api`\nservice must not share a listener with client-facing services, because it\nhas no authentication of its own. Anything you add with worker-level\nprivileges inherits that requirement; see\nsecurity hardening."
  }, {
    "heading": "common-questions",
    "content": "Almost certainly the `srcs` list in `forge-store/BUILD.bazel`. Cargo\nglobs; Bazel enumerates. Add the file, keep the list alphabetical, and\nrun `bazel build //forge-store:forge-store` before pushing."
  }, {
    "heading": "common-questions",
    "content": "Check that the spec struct has\n`#[cfg_attr(feature = \"dev-schema\", derive(JsonSchema))]`. The generated\nreference is produced from the schemars schema, and a struct without that\nderive is invisible to it. If the field is there but has no default,\nadd a `/// Default: …` line to the doc comment."
  }, {
    "heading": "common-questions",
    "content": "Doc comments in `forge-config` are load-bearing twice over: fenced\nJSON blocks are extracted into\n`forge-config/examples/stores-config.json5` by a pre-commit hook,\nand `tests/json5_test.rs` parses every generated example. Malformed JSON\nin a fence fails that test."
  }, {
    "heading": "common-questions",
    "content": "No. Generated Rust is checked into `forge-proto/genproto/`, and\nregeneration goes through `bazel run forge-proto:update_protos`.\nCommit the regenerated files with your change."
  }, {
    "heading": "common-questions",
    "content": "In the implementation, not the config crate; the spec should describe\nintent, and the store applies its own fallback. Record the value in the\nfield's `/// Default:` line so the reference stays honest."
  }, {
    "heading": "common-questions",
    "content": "How the suites are organised, what `#[forge_test]` does for you, and\nwhich local environment problems produce which confusing failure."
  }],
  "headings": [{
    "id": "adding-a-store",
    "content": "Adding a store"
  }, {
    "id": "adding-a-config-field",
    "content": "Adding a config field"
  }, {
    "id": "adding-a-metric",
    "content": "Adding a metric"
  }, {
    "id": "adding-a-grpc-service",
    "content": "Adding a gRPC service"
  }, {
    "id": "common-questions",
    "content": "Common questions"
  }]
};
