  "contents": [{
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "**Who this is for:** anyone with a working cache who wants the misses to stop\nrunning locally. &#x2A;*What you'll have at the end of this section:** a scheduler,\nat least one worker, and a build whose cache misses execute on the farm\ninstead of on your machine. &#x2A;*Time:** an hour for the first remote action,\nlonger if your toolchain isn't hermetic yet."
  }, {
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "A cache serving hits to your build. If you don't have one yet, start with Getting started."
  }, {
    "heading": "what-this-rung-adds",
    "content": "A cache answers the question \"has this exact action already been run?\" When\nthe answer is no, something still has to run it, and with caching alone,\nthat something is your laptop. Remote execution changes the answer to that\nsecond question."
  }, {
    "heading": "what-this-rung-adds",
    "content": "Three things are new in the deployment: a **scheduler** that decides which\nworker gets which action, at least one **worker** that actually runs it, and\nthe **execution service** on the server. One thing is new in your build\ninvocation: you tell the build tool where the executor is, and you declare\nwhat kind of machine your actions need. One thing is deliberately *not* new:\nyour CAS and action cache are exactly the ones Getting started left you with. That's\nwhy the sections are in this order."
  }, {
    "heading": "what-this-rung-adds",
    "content": "From cache to execution is the\nlong version of that paragraph, and it's the page to read first."
  }, {
    "heading": "what-to-expect-the-first-time",
    "content": "The first remote action almost never works on the first try, and it's nearly\nalways one of two walls."
  }, {
    "heading": "what-to-expect-the-first-time",
    "content": "**Platform properties.** The scheduler only hands an action to a worker whose\nadvertised properties satisfy what the action asked for. When they don't line\nup, nothing errors: actions queue, indefinitely, which reads like a hang\nrather than a misconfiguration."
  }, {
    "heading": "what-to-expect-the-first-time",
    "content": "**Toolchain hermeticity.** An action that runs on your machine because your\nmachine happens to have the right compiler will not run on a worker that\ndoesn't. Remote execution turns every implicit dependency on the local\nenvironment into a failure, which is uncomfortable the first time and\nextremely valuable afterwards."
  }, {
    "heading": "what-to-expect-the-first-time",
    "content": "Both walls get their own page here rather than a footnote, because everyone\nhits them."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-pages-in-order",
    "content": "**Understand the change**"
  }, {
    "heading": "the-pages-in-order",
    "content": "From cache to execution:\nwhat execution adds on top of a working cache, what's new in the\ndeployment and the build invocation, and what stays the same."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-pages-in-order",
    "content": "**Get it running**"
  }, {
    "heading": "the-pages-in-order",
    "content": "Your first remote action: a\nscheduler and one worker on your own machine, and a build you can watch\nexecute on them."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-pages-in-order",
    "content": "**Get past the two walls**"
  }, {
    "heading": "the-pages-in-order",
    "content": "Platform properties: the\nmatching contract, why a mismatch queues forever, and the scheduler's own\ndiagnostics."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-pages-in-order",
    "content": "Toolchains and hermeticity:\npinning the toolchain so local and remote actions hash identically."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-pages-in-order",
    "content": "Containers and images: the\nother answer to the same problem, and what `container-image` really does."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-pages-in-order",
    "content": "**Go further**"
  }, {
    "heading": "the-pages-in-order",
    "content": "Persistent workers: pooled\nlong-lived worker processes for toolchains with a startup tax."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-pages-in-order",
    "content": "Local testing: keeping a local cluster\nas a test fixture, in the two shapes the repo itself uses."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-pages-in-order",
    "content": "Examples and templates:\nconfigs, deployment topologies, and project scaffolds to copy."
  }, {
    "heading": "start-here-or-skip-ahead",
    "content": "**Start here** if you have a cache serving hits and haven't run anything\nremotely yet."
