    "heading": "storetype",
    "content": "Description"
  }, {
    "heading": "storetype",
    "content": "`\"cas\"`"
  }, {
    "heading": "storetype",
    "content": "The store is content addressable storage."
  }, {
    "heading": "storetype",
    "content": "`\"ac\"`"
  }, {
    "heading": "storetype",
    "content": "The store is an action cache."
  }, {
    "heading": "storetype",
    "content": "`\"event_sink\"`"
  }, {
    "heading": "storetype",
    "content": "A write-only event sink using `ByteStream.Write`. Only string keys and exact upload sizes are accepted. The resource hash identifies the key, not the payload; the size describes the payload. The upstream must be an event receiver, not a CAS. Reads and existence checks are unsupported. Use this for BEP/origin event forwarding, never for cache data."
  }, {
    "heading": "grpcreadbatchingconfig",
    "content": "Configuration for experimental small-blob read coalescing in a gRPC\nstore. See \\[`GrpcSpec::experimental_read_batching`]."
  }, {
    "heading": "grpcreadbatchingconfig",
    "content": "Field"
  }, {
    "heading": "grpcreadbatchingconfig",
    "content": "Type"
  }, {
    "heading": "grpcreadbatchingconfig",
    "content": "Required"
  }, {
    "heading": "grpcreadbatchingconfig",
    "content": "Default"
  }, {
    "heading": "grpcreadbatchingconfig",
    "content": "Description"
  }, {
    "heading": "grpcreadbatchingconfig",
    "content": "`max_blob_size_bytes`"
  }, {
    "heading": "grpcreadbatchingconfig",
    "content": "integer (uint64)"
  }, {
    "heading": "grpcreadbatchingconfig",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "grpcreadbatchingconfig",
    "content": "131072 (128 KiB)"
  }, {
    "heading": "grpcreadbatchingconfig",
    "content": "Only blobs at or below this size (in bytes) are eligible for batching. Larger blobs always use the `ByteStream` `Read` path."
  }, {
    "heading": "grpcreadbatchingconfig",
    "content": "`max_batch_bytes`"
  }, {
    "heading": "grpcreadbatchingconfig",
    "content": "integer (uint64)"
  }, {
    "heading": "grpcreadbatchingconfig",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "grpcreadbatchingconfig",
    "content": "3145728 (3 MiB)"
  }, {
    "heading": "grpcreadbatchingconfig",
    "content": "Maximum total payload bytes packed into a single `BatchReadBlobs` request. This should leave headroom under the 4 MiB default gRPC message limit for protobuf framing overhead."
  }, {
    "heading": "grpcreadbatchingconfig",
    "content": "`dispatch_slots`"
  }, {
    "heading": "grpcreadbatchingconfig",
    "content": "integer (uint)"
  }, {
    "heading": "grpcreadbatchingconfig",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "grpcreadbatchingconfig",
    "content": "4"
  }, {
    "heading": "grpcreadbatchingconfig",
    "content": "Maximum number of concurrent `BatchReadBlobs` RPCs dispatched by the coalescer. Must be greater than zero."
  }, {
    "heading": "grpcreadbatchingconfig",
    "content": "`max_queued_bytes`"
  }, {
    "heading": "grpcreadbatchingconfig",
    "content": "integer (uint64)"
  }, {
    "heading": "grpcreadbatchingconfig",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "grpcreadbatchingconfig",
    "content": "33554432 (32 MiB)"
  }, {
    "heading": "grpcreadbatchingconfig",
    "content": "Bound on the number of payload bytes waiting in the coalescer queue. When exceeded, new read requests bypass batching and fall back to the regular `ByteStream` `Read` path instead of blocking."
  }, {
