  }, {
    "heading": "endpointconfig",
    "content": "`timeout`"
  }, {
    "heading": "endpointconfig",
    "content": "number (float)"
  }, {
    "heading": "endpointconfig",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "endpointconfig",
    "content": "5 seconds"
  }, {
    "heading": "endpointconfig",
    "content": "Timeout in seconds for connecting to the endpoint and for a request to be answered. The worker's messages to the scheduler (keepalives, acknowledgements, results) ride on the one `ConnectWorker` stream opened at registration, which this does not bound; the `GoingAway` sent at shutdown is bounded by it, so a stalled connection cannot hold a pod past its grace period. A keepalive goes out every half of it."
  }, {
    "heading": "endpointconfig",
    "content": "`tcp_keepalive_s`"
  }, {
    "heading": "endpointconfig",
    "content": "integer (uint64)"
  }, {
    "heading": "endpointconfig",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "endpointconfig",
    "content": "30 seconds"
  }, {
    "heading": "endpointconfig",
    "content": "TCP keepalive interval (seconds), probing the socket under the scheduler connection so a dead peer is noticed at the OS level."
  }, {
    "heading": "endpointconfig",
    "content": "`http2_keepalive_interval_s`"
  }, {
    "heading": "endpointconfig",
    "content": "integer (uint64)"
  }, {
    "heading": "endpointconfig",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "endpointconfig",
    "content": "30 seconds"
  }, {
    "heading": "endpointconfig",
    "content": "HTTP/2 keepalive interval (seconds): PING frames on the scheduler connection, so one that has gone dead underneath fails instead of hanging every message on it."
  }, {
    "heading": "endpointconfig",
    "content": "`http2_keepalive_timeout_s`"
  }, {
    "heading": "endpointconfig",
    "content": "integer (uint64)"
  }, {
    "heading": "endpointconfig",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "endpointconfig",
    "content": "20 seconds"
  }, {
    "heading": "endpointconfig",
    "content": "HTTP/2 keepalive timeout (seconds): a PING unanswered for this long ends the connection, and the worker reconnects."
  }, {
