  }, {
    "heading": "buck2filecaptureconfig",
    "content": "Opt-in file capture for the actual container executing a Buck2 action.\nRequires a fresh single-use container with no outer execution wrapper or\nseparate action mount namespace. For nested runtimes, run `Forge` and the\ncapture helper inside the execution container. Other build tools never start\ncapture. The helper uploads an archive before `Forge` cleans up the action."
  }, {
    "heading": "buck2filecaptureconfig",
    "content": "The operator supplies the helper executable and its authenticated ingest\nservice. `Forge` sends one JSON record on stdin and expects `ready\\n`\non stdout within 30 seconds. Closing stdin requests final capture; the helper\nmust exit only after durable acknowledgement, or exit unsuccessfully if the\narchive is partial. See `forge-worker/README.md` for the control protocol."
  }, {
