    "heading": "memoryescalationspec",
    "content": "string"
  }, {
    "heading": "memoryescalationspec",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "memoryescalationspec",
    "content": "`memory_kb`"
  }, {
    "heading": "memoryescalationspec",
    "content": "The `minimum` platform property carrying the memory reservation."
  }, {
    "heading": "memoryescalationspec",
    "content": "`percent`"
  }, {
    "heading": "memoryescalationspec",
    "content": "integer (uint64)"
  }, {
    "heading": "memoryescalationspec",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "memoryescalationspec",
    "content": "200"
  }, {
    "heading": "memoryescalationspec",
    "content": "Each kill scales the reservation by this factor, in hundredths: 200 doubles it, 150 adds half."
  }, {
    "heading": "memoryescalationspec",
    "content": "`max_kb`"
  }, {
    "heading": "memoryescalationspec",
    "content": "integer (uint64)"
  }, {
    "heading": "memoryescalationspec",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "memoryescalationspec",
    "content": "0"
  }, {
    "heading": "memoryescalationspec",
    "content": "Never reserve more than this many KiB; 0 takes the largest memory any connected worker advertises."
  }, {
    "heading": "memoryescalationspec",
    "content": "`ladder_kb`"
  }, {
    "heading": "memoryescalationspec",
    "content": "array of integer (uint64)"
  }, {
    "heading": "memoryescalationspec",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "memoryescalationspec",
    "content": "empty (scale by `percent`)"
  }, {
    "heading": "memoryescalationspec",
    "content": "The memory values of the fleet's size classes, ascending, in KiB. When set, a kill steps the reservation to the next class above it instead of scaling by `percent`; past the top class the last step reserves the largest worker whole. The chart fills this from the same classes the `historical_resource` scheduler uses."
  }, {
    "heading": "memoryescalationspec",
    "content": "`cpu_property`"
  }, {
    "heading": "memoryescalationspec",
    "content": "string"
  }, {
    "heading": "memoryescalationspec",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "memoryescalationspec",
    "content": "`cpu_count`"
  }, {
    "heading": "memoryescalationspec",
    "content": "The `minimum` platform property carrying the CPU reservation. The last escalation reserves the largest worker's whole memory and, through this property, its whole CPU, so nothing shares the worker with the action. Empty leaves CPU alone."
  }, {
    "heading": "memoryescalationspec",
    "content": "`max_steps`"
  }, {
    "heading": "memoryescalationspec",
    "content": "integer (uint64)"
  }, {
    "heading": "memoryescalationspec",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "memoryescalationspec",
    "content": "8"
  }, {
    "heading": "memoryescalationspec",
    "content": "The most escalations one action gets before the scheduler completes it with `FailedPrecondition`; 0 lets the ceiling alone bound them."
  }, {
    "heading": "experimentalsimpleschedulerbackend",
    "content": "One of:"
  }, {
    "heading": "experimentalsimpleschedulerbackend",
    "content": "`\"memory\"` — Use an in-memory store for the scheduler."
  }, {
    "heading": "experimentalsimpleschedulerbackend",
    "content": "`redis`: ExperimentalRedisSchedulerBackend — Use a Redis store for the scheduler."
