    "heading": "workerapiconfig",
    "content": "Yes"
  }, {
    "heading": "workerapiconfig",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "workerapiconfig",
    "content": "The scheduler name referenced in the `schedulers` map in the main config."
  }, {
    "heading": "workerapiconfig",
    "content": "`disable_kill_revoked_operations`"
  }, {
    "heading": "workerapiconfig",
    "content": "boolean"
  }, {
    "heading": "workerapiconfig",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "workerapiconfig",
    "content": "false (the sweep runs)"
  }, {
    "heading": "workerapiconfig",
    "content": "Disable the periodic sweep that tells workers to kill operations the scheduler no longer has executing on them (for example because every client disconnected before the action finished). With the sweep disabled such orphaned actions run to completion and still warm the action cache, which can be preferable for deployments with long or expensive actions whose clients merely retry."
  }, {
    "heading": "workerapiconfig",
    "content": "`kill_revoked_operations_interval_s`"
  }, {
    "heading": "workerapiconfig",
    "content": "integer (uint64)"
  }, {
    "heading": "workerapiconfig",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "workerapiconfig",
    "content": "5 (0 uses the default)"
  }, {
    "heading": "workerapiconfig",
    "content": "How often, in seconds, the scheduler checks for operations that are still running on a worker but are no longer executing according to the state manager, and tells the worker to kill them. Each pass costs one state-manager lookup per running operation, so store-backed deployments with many concurrent actions may want a longer interval."
  }, {
