  "contents": [{
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "**Who this is for:** maintainers cutting a release, and anyone who needs to\nknow what a version number means before pinning one. &#x2A;*What you'll have at\nthe end:** the fourteen files a version lives in, the release sequence, what\neach workflow produces, and the compatibility policy, which is mostly the\nabsence of one. &#x2A;*Time:** twenty minutes."
  }, {
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "Forge's release process is deliberately semi-manual. Tags are signed by\na human, and release notes are written by a human, because both are things\nan automated changelog does badly. Everything downstream of the tag is\nautomated."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-version-lives-in-fourteen-files",
