    "heading": "the-version-lives-in-fourteen-files",
    "content": "1"
  }, {
    "heading": "the-version-lives-in-fourteen-files",
    "content": "The macro-derive crate is nested one level deeper inside\n`forge-metric/` and does not match a `forge-*/Cargo.toml` glob.\n`CONTRIBUTING.md` calls it out by name and gives a sanity check: a standard\nrelease commit touches 17 files, the fourteen above plus `Cargo.lock`,\n`forge-test/fuzz/Cargo.lock` and `CHANGELOG.md`."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-version-lives-in-fourteen-files",
    "content": "Several things that contain a version are **generated** and must not be\nhand-edited: `CHANGELOG.md` (git-cliff, configured by `cliff.toml`),\n`web/apps/docs/lib/config-versions.ts`, the per-version configuration\nreference pages, and the lockfiles."
  }, {
    "heading": "cutting-a-release",
    "content": "The authoritative sequence is the numbered list under \"Creating releases\" in\n.\nThe shape of it:"
  }, {
    "heading": "cutting-a-release",
    "content": "**Bump the version** in all fourteen files."
  }, {
    "heading": "cutting-a-release",
    "content": "**Prepend the new changelog section**, after `git fetch upstream --tags`\nso `--unreleased` means what it should:\n`git cliff --unreleased --tag=v1.x.y --prepend CHANGELOG.md`. Do not\nregenerate the whole file; that rewrites earlier entries and drops manual\ncuration. Adjusting `cliff.toml` is expected when a commit lands in the\nwrong section."
  }, {
    "heading": "cutting-a-release",
    "content": "**Open the release PR**, titled `Release Forge v1.x.y`, and merge it."
  }, {
    "heading": "cutting-a-release",
    "content": "**Create a signed tag on the release commit**: `git tag -s v1.x.y`, with\nthe tag message equal to the tag name. Use the `v<major>.<minor>.<patch>`\nform: the image workflow fires on any tag, but the config-reference\nworkflow only fires on `v1.*`."
  }, {
    "heading": "cutting-a-release",
    "content": "**Push the tag to your fork first.** That triggers the image workflow in\nyour own repository, which is the dry run. Only push to `upstream` once\nit is green."
  }, {
    "heading": "cutting-a-release",
    "content": "**Confirm the config reference regenerated.** Pushing the tag upstream\ntriggers `config-reference.yaml`, which opens an auto-merging PR against\n`main`. If it did not fire, re-run it from the Actions tab or regenerate\nby hand with\n`bun --filter @forge/docs gen:config-reference v1.x.y`."
  }, {
    "heading": "cutting-a-release",
    "content": "**Write the release notes**, attributing every entry to its author, then\npublish. Publishing is what triggers the signed-artifacts workflow."
  }, {
    "heading": "cutting-a-release",
    "content": "**Verify the assets landed**: for each target, a `.tar.gz` plus its\n`.sig` and `.pem`, an `.spdx.json` SBOM, and an `.intoto.jsonl`\nprovenance file."
  }, {
    "heading": "what-the-tag-triggers",
