    "heading": "actions-queue-forever-and-workers-sit-idle",
    "content": "The single most important asymmetry in Forge:"
  }, {
    "heading": "actions-queue-forever-and-workers-sit-idle",
    "content": "If your action names a platform property that is **not** in the scheduler's\n`supported_platform_properties`, you get an immediate `InvalidArgument`:"
  }, {
    "heading": "actions-queue-forever-and-workers-sit-idle",
    "content": "If the property name is known but **no worker advertises a satisfying\nvalue**, the scheduler's matching pass returns without doing anything.\nThe action stays `Queued`. Nothing escalates, nothing times out, nothing is\nlogged above `INFO`."
  }, {
    "heading": "actions-queue-forever-and-workers-sit-idle",
    "content": "That second case is not a bug so much as a consequence of how matching works\n(\"no worker matches yet\" is indistinguishable from \"no worker matches ever\"),\nbut its operational effect is a build that hangs with no diagnostic."
  }, {
    "heading": "actions-queue-forever-and-workers-sit-idle",
    "content": "`max_action_executing_timeout_s` does not help, because it applies only to the\n`Executing` state and the action never reaches it. The only thing that ever\nends the wait is `client_action_timeout_s` (default 60 s) noticing the client\nhas stopped listening, which produces a message about\nclients listening and says\nnothing about properties."
  }, {
    "heading": "diagnose-it",
    "content": "Raise the log level. Every useful diagnostic here is at `INFO`, and the shipped\nexamples run at `warn`."
  }, {
