    "heading": "worker-connection-churn",
    "content": "A worker that logs at a steady \\~2 Hz is reconnecting:"
  }, {
    "heading": "worker-connection-churn",
    "content": "Reconnect is a **flat 0.5-second retry: no backoff, no jitter, no cap, and no\nconfiguration field**. That cadence is the signature, and a scheduler outage\nproduces it from every worker simultaneously for the duration."
  }, {
    "heading": "worker-connection-churn",
    "content": "Every reconnect calls `kill_all()`, destroying every in-flight action on that\nworker. If your builds are failing intermittently and your workers are\nchurning, those are the same incident."
  }, {
    "heading": "worker-connection-churn",
    "content": "String"
  }, {
    "heading": "worker-connection-churn",
    "content": "Meaning"
  }, {
    "heading": "worker-connection-churn",
    "content": "`Worker registered with scheduler`"
  }, {
    "heading": "worker-connection-churn",
    "content": "The handshake succeeded."
  }, {
    "heading": "worker-connection-churn",
    "content": "`Worker disconnected from scheduler`"
  }, {
    "heading": "worker-connection-churn",
    "content": "The stream broke; `kill_all()` is about to run."
  }, {
    "heading": "worker-connection-churn",
    "content": "`Actions in transit did not reach zero before we disconnected from the scheduler`"
  }, {
    "heading": "worker-connection-churn",
    "content": "The 10-second drain window expired with work still in flight."
  }, {
    "heading": "worker-connection-churn",
    "content": "`Worker <id> timed out, removing from pool`"
  }, {
    "heading": "worker-connection-churn",
    "content": "Scheduler side. A worker is only evicted when both its local timestamp and the worker registry agree it is dead."
  }, {
    "heading": "worker-connection-churn",
    "content": "`Worker command failed, removing worker <id>`"
  }, {
    "heading": "worker-connection-churn",
    "content": "The scheduler could not deliver work to it."
  }, {
    "heading": "worker-connection-churn",
    "content": "The worker sends a keepalive every half of its `worker_api_endpoint.timeout`\n(default 5 s, so every 2.5 s), and the scheduler evicts a worker it has not\nheard from for `worker_timeout_s` (default 10 s), checking once a second. Any\nmessage from the worker resets that clock, not only keepalives. The\nscheduler counts what it receives in `forge_worker_keepalives_total` and\ndepartures by reason in `forge_worker_disconnections_total`."
  }, {
    "heading": "limits-that-block-instead-of-erroring",
    "content": "If the symptom is \"everything got slow and nothing errored\", you are probably\nsitting on one of these:"
  }, {
    "heading": "limits-that-block-instead-of-erroring",
    "content": "Limit"
  }, {
    "heading": "limits-that-block-instead-of-erroring",
    "content": "Default"
  }, {
    "heading": "limits-that-block-instead-of-erroring",
    "content": "Behaviour"
  }, {
    "heading": "limits-that-block-instead-of-erroring",
    "content": "Open file descriptors"
  }, {
    "heading": "limits-that-block-instead-of-erroring",
    "content": "24576"
  }, {
    "heading": "limits-that-block-instead-of-erroring",
    "content": "Blocks on a semaphore. &#x2A;*Never produces `EMFILE`.**"
  }, {
    "heading": "limits-that-block-instead-of-erroring",
    "content": "`max_concurrent_requests` (gRPC)"
  }, {
    "heading": "limits-that-block-instead-of-erroring",
    "content": "unlimited"
  }, {
    "heading": "limits-that-block-instead-of-erroring",
    "content": "Queues rather than rejecting."
  }, {
    "heading": "limits-that-block-instead-of-erroring",
    "content": "`max_client_permits` (Redis)"
  }, {
