  }, {
    "heading": "limits-that-block-instead-of-erroring",
    "content": "Blocks when set."
  }, {
    "heading": "limits-that-block-instead-of-erroring",
    "content": "The FD limit deserves special attention. Forge uses only **80% of the\nlimit it actually achieved**, not 80% of what you configured. In a container\nwith a hard `nofile` cap, the semaphore silently shrinks and the only evidence\nis a startup warning:"
  }, {
    "heading": "limits-that-block-instead-of-erroring",
    "content": "Or, if the raise failed entirely:"
  }, {
    "heading": "limits-that-block-instead-of-erroring",
    "content": "Every filesystem operation takes a permit: opens, creates, hard links, chmod,\ndirectory creation, directory reads, symlink reads. When permits run out,\neverything using the filesystem store queues."
  }, {
    "heading": "startup-failures",
    "content": "These all abort the process before it serves anything. All of them are config\nwiring, and all of them name the offending key."
  }, {
