    "heading": "startup-failures",
    "content": "Index store name typo."
  }, {
    "heading": "startup-failures",
    "content": "`'redis_store': '<name>' does not exist`"
  }, {
    "heading": "startup-failures",
    "content": "Scheduler backend points at an undefined store."
  }, {
    "heading": "startup-failures",
    "content": "`Could not downcast to redis store in RedisAwaitedActionDb::new`"
  }, {
    "heading": "startup-failures",
    "content": "The referenced store is not a standard-mode Redis store."
  }, {
    "heading": "startup-failures",
    "content": "`No addresses were specified in redis store configuration.`"
  }, {
    "heading": "startup-failures",
    "content": "Empty `addresses`."
  }, {
    "heading": "startup-failures",
    "content": "`Both connection_timeout_s and connection_timeout_ms were set, can only have one!`"
  }, {
    "heading": "startup-failures",
    "content": "Pick the `_ms` form; the `_s` form is deprecated."
  }, {
    "heading": "startup-failures",
    "content": "`upload_ac_results_strategy is set, but no ac_store is configured`"
  }, {
    "heading": "startup-failures",
    "content": "The worker will upload action results but has nowhere to put them."
  }, {
    "heading": "startup-failures",
    "content": "`Could not remove work_directory '<path>' in LocalWorker`"
  }, {
    "heading": "startup-failures",
    "content": "The worker purges its work directory at startup and could not. Two workers sharing one work directory is the usual cause."
  }, {
    "heading": "startup-failures",
    "content": "Config parsing uses `deny_unknown_fields`, so a misspelled key is a startup\nerror naming the key, not a silently ignored setting. That is a feature; trust\nthe message."
  }, {
    "heading": "startup-failures",
    "content": "One string that looks like a startup failure and is not:\n`Could not parse the value of precondition_script: '<v>'`. The\n`experimental_precondition_script` value is split with `shlex` before every\naction, not at startup, so an unparseable value fails each action as it\narrives and the worker stays up."
  }, {
    "heading": "retries",
    "content": "Retry exhaustion is **not** a distinct error. It is the last underlying error\nwith a suffix appended:"
  }, {
    "heading": "retries",
    "content": "The code and message you see are the *cause*, and the suffix tells you it\nhad been happening repeatedly."
  }, {
    "heading": "retries",
    "content": "Non-retryable codes: `InvalidArgument`, `FailedPrecondition`, `OutOfRange`,\n`Unimplemented`, `NotFound`, `AlreadyExists`, `PermissionDenied`,\n`Unauthenticated`. Everything else retries, which is why a full disk, arriving\nas `Unknown` or `Internal`, burns the whole retry budget before failing."
  }, {
    "heading": "retries",
    "content": "Two other retry strings: `Retry stream ended abruptly on attempt N`, and\n`Not retrying permanent error`."
  }, {
    "heading": "where-else-to-look",
    "content": "Scaling workers has a \"when it doesn't work\"\nsection covering the fleet-shaped versions of several problems above: queue\ndepth high while workers idle, adding workers not helping, scale-in causing\nfailed actions, two workers on one host behaving erratically. It complements\nthis page rather than duplicating it."
  }, {
    "heading": "where-else-to-look",
    "content": "Observability covers the metrics\npipeline itself: no metrics appearing, missing cache metrics, out-of-order\nsamples. Note that those are problems with the *collector*, not with\nForge."
  }, {
    "heading": "where-else-to-look",
    "content": "Security hardening covers what is deliberately\nabsent rather than broken: there is no inbound authentication anywhere, and\nthe committed certificates expired in 2024."
  }, {
    "heading": "whats-next",
    "content": "Once you know which incident you are in, the procedure that ends it."
  }, {
    "heading": "whats-next",
    "content": "Every field, every default, generated from the source."
  }, {
    "heading": "whats-next",
    "content": "The levers that make a healthy system faster."
  }],
