export let structuredData = {
  "contents": [{
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "**Who this is for:** anyone deciding what a Forge process should expose,\nand on which port. &#x2A;*What you'll know at the end:** what a listener is, what\neach of the eleven services does, how `instance_name` partitions a cache, and\nwhy the worker API must not share a port with anything else. &#x2A;*Time:** thirty\nminutes."
  }, {
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "Named stores you can refer to. See Stores."
  }, {
    "heading": "a-server-is-a-listener-plus-a-set-of-services",
    "content": "The `servers` array is the only entry point into a Forge process.\nEach entry binds one socket and decides what is reachable on it:"
  }, {
    "heading": "a-server-is-a-listener-plus-a-set-of-services",
    "content": "Four things are going on there, and each is worth naming."
  }, {
    "heading": "a-server-is-a-listener-plus-a-set-of-services",
    "content": "`name` is documented as a label for telemetry and logs, defaulting to the\nserver's index in the array. Set it; it's the cheapest documentation in the\nfile."
  }, {
    "heading": "a-server-is-a-listener-plus-a-set-of-services",
    "content": "`listener` currently has exactly one variant, `http`, which serves\nHTTP/HTTP2 and therefore gRPC. `socket_address` is parsed as a Rust\n`SocketAddr`, so it must be an IP literal plus port: `0.0.0.0:50051` to bind\nevery IPv4 interface, `[::]:50051` for IPv6, `127.0.0.1:50051` for loopback\nonly. A hostname or a bare `:port` is rejected as an invalid address. TLS,\nHTTP/2 tuning, and compression are options on the listener, not on the\nservices."
  }, {
    "heading": "a-server-is-a-listener-plus-a-set-of-services",
    "content": "`services` is optional in the schema, but the binary refuses to start a\nserver without it (`'services' must be configured`), so in practice every\nserver entry carries one."
  }, {
    "heading": "a-server-is-a-listener-plus-a-set-of-services",
    "content": "Each service entry names a store or a scheduler as a **string**, the name\nfrom the `stores` or `schedulers` array. This is where the wiring described in\nthe section overview actually happens."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-eleven-services",
    "content": "Service"
  }, {
    "heading": "the-eleven-services",
    "content": "What it serves"
  }, {
    "heading": "the-eleven-services",
    "content": "Wants"
  }, {
    "heading": "the-eleven-services",
    "content": "`cas`"
  }, {
    "heading": "the-eleven-services",
    "content": "REAPI `ContentAddressableStorage`: blob upload and lookup"
  }, {
    "heading": "the-eleven-services",
    "content": "`cas_store`"
  }, {
    "heading": "the-eleven-services",
    "content": "`ac`"
  }, {
    "heading": "the-eleven-services",
    "content": "REAPI `ActionCache`: cached action results"
  }, {
    "heading": "the-eleven-services",
    "content": "`ac_store`"
  }, {
    "heading": "the-eleven-services",
    "content": "`bytestream`"
  }, {
    "heading": "the-eleven-services",
    "content": "Streaming reads and writes for large blobs"
  }, {
    "heading": "the-eleven-services",
    "content": "`cas_store`"
  }, {
    "heading": "the-eleven-services",
    "content": "`capabilities`"
  }, {
    "heading": "the-eleven-services",
    "content": "What this endpoint supports; required by Bazel"
  }, {
    "heading": "the-eleven-services",
    "content": "optionally a scheduler"
  }, {
    "heading": "the-eleven-services",
    "content": "`execution`"
  }, {
    "heading": "the-eleven-services",
    "content": "REAPI `Execution`: accepts `Execute` calls"
  }, {
    "heading": "the-eleven-services",
    "content": "`cas_store` and `scheduler`"
  }, {
    "heading": "the-eleven-services",
    "content": "`fetch`"
  }, {
    "heading": "the-eleven-services",
    "content": "Remote Asset protocol, fetch half"
  }, {
    "heading": "the-eleven-services",
