  "title": "Develop with Bazel",
  "description": "Build, test, and run Forge with Bazel, the same dev loop CI uses."
};
export let structuredData = {
  "contents": [{
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "The Bazel-based dev loop is the one our CI runs. Use this if you want\nthe most reproducible setup or if your editor integration prefers\nBazel."
  }, {
    "heading": "prerequisites",
    "content": "Bazelisk, which reads `.bazelversion` and fetches the right Bazel for\nyou. CI runs 9.1.1 and also checks 8.7.0."
  }, {
    "heading": "prerequisites",
    "content": "A C++ toolchain (clang or gcc) for native dependencies."
  }, {
    "heading": "prerequisites",
    "content": "On macOS: XCode command-line tools."
  }, {
    "heading": "prerequisites",
    "content": "On Linux, inside the Nix shell, the LRE toolchains link with `mold`;\noutside it Bazel uses whatever the host toolchain provides."
  }, {
    "heading": "first-build",
    "content": "The first `bazel test` will take 10-20 minutes as it builds the\ntoolchain and dependencies. Subsequent builds finish in seconds."
  }, {
    "heading": "first-build",
    "content": "`.bazelrc` already defines `--config=self_test` (remote cache at\n`grpc://127.0.0.1:50051`) and `--config=self_execute` (remote executor at\n`grpc://127.0.0.1:50052`) for a Forge running locally. For any other\nendpoint, put the flags in `user.bazelrc` at the repository root, which\n`.bazelrc` pulls in with `try-import` and git ignores:"
  }, {
    "heading": "first-build",
    "content": "With a Forge cluster running, subsequent builds will hit the cache\nfor any action your team has already produced."
  }, {
    "heading": "common-commands",
    "content": "See the testing guide for what `unit_test`\nand `integration` actually mean in this repository; they do not mean what\nthe names suggest."
  }, {
    "heading": "editor-integration",
    "content": "For `rust-analyzer`:"
  }, {
    "heading": "editor-integration",
    "content": "This generates a `rust-project.json` that VS Code / Helix / your\neditor of choice will pick up."
  }, {
    "heading": "common-pitfalls",
    "content": "**LRE flags are missing**: `.bazelrc` pulls in `lre.bazelrc`,\n`forge.bazelrc`, `nixos.bazelrc` and `darwin.bazelrc` with\n`try-import`, and the Nix dev shell is what generates them. Without\n`nix develop` they do not exist, and the `try-` means Bazel\nsays nothing about it. See Develop with Nix."
  }, {
    "heading": "common-pitfalls",
    "content": "**Slow first build with no cache**: expected. Subsequent builds\nreuse Bazel's local cache; pointing at a remote Forge cluster\nmakes a fresh clone fast for everyone."
  }, {
    "heading": "common-pitfalls",
    "content": "**A new source file builds with Cargo and fails under Bazel**: Bazel\nenumerates `srcs` rather than globbing. Add the file to the crate's\n`BUILD.bazel`, alphabetically."
  }, {
    "heading": "faq",
    "content": "It bootstraps the toolchain and builds every dependency from source.\nSubsequent builds are seconds, and pointing `--remote_cache` at a\nForge cluster (above) makes even a fresh clone fast."
  }, {
    "heading": "faq",
    "content": "No. Target what you touched\n(`bazel test //forge-store:integration`), then run the\nfull `bazel test //...` once before submitting."
  }, {
    "heading": "faq",
    "content": "For non-Bazel workflows, see\nDevelop with Cargo or\nDevelop with Nix."
  }],
  "headings": [{
    "id": "prerequisites",
