    "heading": "where-tests-live",
    "content": "2"
  }, {
    "heading": "where-tests-live",
    "content": "A new test file has to be added to its crate's `rust_test_suite` in\n`BUILD.bazel`. Cargo picks it up automatically; Bazel does not."
  }, {
    "heading": "forge-test",
    "content": "Around 780 tests use it. It is defined in"
  }, {
    "heading": "forge-test",
    "content": "and it is not a thin wrapper; it expands to five things:"
  }, {
    "heading": "forge-test",
    "content": "`#[tokio::test]`, so the test body can be `async`"
  }, {
    "heading": "forge-test",
    "content": "`#[::tracing_test::traced_test]`, capturing logs for assertions"
  }, {
    "heading": "forge-test",
    "content": "an `error_span!` named after the test function"
  }, {
    "heading": "forge-test",
    "content": "`reseed_rng_for_test()`, so randomised tests are reproducible"
  }, {
    "heading": "forge-test",
    "content": "a **log-redaction assertion** that fails the test if any captured log line\ncontains `\" data: b\"` (with one carve-out for an `aws_runtime` line that\nlegitimately does)"
  }, {
    "heading": "forge-test",
    "content": "That last one is the surprising one. It exists to catch blob contents\nleaking into debug output. If your test starts failing with\n`Non-redacted data in \"...\"` and you did not change any assertion, something\nyou touched is now logging a `Debug` of a buffer."
  }, {
    "heading": "forge-test",
    "content": "The forms:"
  }, {
    "heading": "fixtures-that-already-exist",
    "content": "Reach for these before writing your own."
  }, {
    "heading": "fixtures-that-already-exist",
    "content": "**Redis**: `forge-redis-tester` provides a fake Redis, a `MockPubSub`,\nand a read-only Redis wrapper. Note that it is a regular dependency of\n`forge-store`, not a dev-dependency."
  }, {
    "heading": "fixtures-that-already-exist",
    "content": "**Time**: `MockInstantWrapped` plus `mock_instant::MockClock::advance` lets\nyou move a store's clock forward without sleeping. Combine with\n`#[forge_test(start_paused = true)]` for Tokio's virtual time."
  }, {
    "heading": "fixtures-that-already-exist",
    "content": "**Scheduler helpers**: `forge-scheduler/tests/utils/scheduler_utils.rs`,\npulled in with an inline `mod utils { pub(crate) mod scheduler_utils; }`\nblock rather than as a crate."
  }, {
    "heading": "fixtures-that-already-exist",
    "content": "**Mongo**: `forge-store/tests/mongo_runner/` downloads and starts a\nreal `mongod`. This is why the store crate's Bazel timeout is `moderate`\nrather than `short`, and why that suite needs network on a cold cache."
  }, {
    "heading": "fixtures-that-already-exist",
    "content": "**Temp paths**: `make_temp_path` honours `TEST_TMPDIR`, so tests behave\nunder Bazel's sandbox."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-end-to-end-suites",
    "content": "It refuses to run as root, requires Bazel, Docker and `sudo`, and waits for\nports 50051, 50052 and 50071 before starting. It drives\n`simple_cache_test.sh`, `simple_remote_execution_test.sh`,\n`simple_tls_test.sh` and `chunking_cache_test.sh`. You can pass a pattern to\nrun one of them."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-end-to-end-suites",
    "content": "Beyond those, `integration_tests/` also holds BuildStream, Buck2 and Mongo\nsuites driven from Nix, and `forge-test/fuzz` holds a single fuzz\ntarget (`cas_config.rs`) run by ClusterFuzzLite."
  }, {
    "heading": "coverage",
    "content": "The `result` symlink contains an HTML report. **No coverage\nthreshold gate**; no PR is blocked on a percentage. Coverage is a tool for\nfinding untested paths, not a target to hit."
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-fails-locally-but-not-in-ci",
    "content": "Most of these are environment, not code."
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-fails-locally-but-not-in-ci",
    "content": "Symptom"
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-fails-locally-but-not-in-ci",
