    "heading": "when-it-fails-locally-but-not-in-ci",
    "content": "`run_integration_tests.sh` exits immediately"
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-fails-locally-but-not-in-ci",
    "content": "Running as root, or Docker not reachable without `sudo`"
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-fails-locally-but-not-in-ci",
    "content": "Run as a non-root user with Docker access"
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-fails-locally-but-not-in-ci",
    "content": "The Mongo store suite times out"
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-fails-locally-but-not-in-ci",
    "content": "It downloads a real `mongod` on a cold Bazel cache"
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-fails-locally-but-not-in-ci",
    "content": "Give it network, and don't run it on a plane"
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-fails-locally-but-not-in-ci",
    "content": "Two tests pass alone, fail together"
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-fails-locally-but-not-in-ci",
    "content": "Both touch process environment; they are marked `#[serial(env)]` for a reason"
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-fails-locally-but-not-in-ci",
    "content": "Don't parallelise them, and mark new env-touching tests the same way"
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-fails-locally-but-not-in-ci",
    "content": "`Non-redacted data in \"...\"`"
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-fails-locally-but-not-in-ci",
    "content": "The `#[forge_test]` log assertion caught new `Debug` output containing a buffer"
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-fails-locally-but-not-in-ci",
    "content": "Redact the log line rather than the assertion"
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-fails-locally-but-not-in-ci",
    "content": "Formatting failures from `bazel test`"
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-fails-locally-but-not-in-ci",
    "content": "Stable `cargo fmt` ignores the nightly-only rustfmt options"
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-fails-locally-but-not-in-ci",
    "content": "`bazel run --config=rustfmt @rules_rust//:rustfmt`"
  }, {
    "heading": "common-questions",
    "content": "Run the crate you touched with Cargo while iterating, then\n`bazel test //...` once before pushing. CI runs Bazel, and the aspects\nattached to `bazel test` catch formatting and clippy problems that a\nCargo run does not."
  }, {
    "heading": "common-questions",
    "content": "Doc comments in `forge-config` are the source text for the generated\nconfiguration reference, so their examples\nare user-facing documentation. `bazel test doctests` is what stops them\nrotting."
  }, {
    "heading": "common-questions",
    "content": "No. Use `#[forge_test(start_paused = true)]` with Tokio's virtual\nclock, or `MockInstantWrapped` with `MockClock::advance` where a store's\nown clock is what matters. A real sleep makes the suite slower and\nflakier at the same time."
  }, {
    "heading": "common-questions",
    "content": "No numeric gate exists. What reviewers ask for is a regression test for\na bug fix and both unit and integration coverage for new behaviour; see\ncontribution guidelines."
  }, {
    "heading": "common-questions",
    "content": "In the crate's `BUILD.bazel`, in the `srcs` list of its `rust_test_suite`\n(named `integration`). Cargo discovers `tests/*.rs` automatically, so a\ntest that runs locally and never runs in CI is usually this."
  }, {
    "heading": "common-questions",
    "content": "How a version becomes a tag, what the tag triggers, and what compatibility\nForge does and does not promise."
  }],
