      children: ["Development builds also support ", _jsx(_components.code, {
        children: "grpc.store_type: \"event_sink\""
      }), " for forwarding\nBEP and origin events to a dedicated receiver. This mode accepts string keys\nwith exact payload sizes and sends uncompressed ", _jsx(_components.code, {
        children: "ByteStream.Write"
      }), " requests.\nThe resource hash identifies the event key, while the size describes the event\nbytes. Configure it only as an event publisher's store: reads, existence checks,\nand digest-key writes are rejected. A normal CAS endpoint cannot receive these\nwrites. The receiver must acknowledge the full payload size only after its\ndurable append completes; Forge rejects a different committed size, and\nits BEP response waits for that acknowledgement. A lost acknowledgement can\ncause a retry after the receiver has already persisted an event. The receiver\nmust use the stable event key to detect and ignore duplicate events, including\nretries that start a new upload; the upload UUID alone is not an event identity.\nOrigin publishing retains its existing bounded retry policy. This transport\nprovides neither exactly-once processing nor a durable publisher recovery ledger."]
