  "contents": [{
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "**Who this is for:** anyone who wants durability they don't operate, on S3 or\nsomething that speaks S3. &#x2A;*What you'll have at the end:** a bucket-backed CAS\nbehind a local fast tier, with credentials that aren't in the config file.\n&#x2A;*Time:** thirty minutes, most of it bucket and IAM setup."
  }, {
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "A config file you can edit (see Configuration), and a bucket you can write to."
  }, {
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "Three providers share one store type and one block of common options. `aws`\nand `r2` share one implementation (R2 is the S3 store with a derived endpoint\nand region `auto`); `ontap` has its own, with a few differences noted below.\nThey differ mainly in how the endpoint and credentials are derived:"
