    "heading": "persistent-workers-activate-from-the-action-not-from-your-config",
    "content": "Those properties come from your build tool. Bazel sets them on rules that\ndeclare worker support: Java and Scala compilation, TypeScript, and anything\nusing `ctx.actions.run` with `execution_requirements` asking for workers.\nA Bazel build that already uses persistent workers locally will exercise\nthe licensed module remotely the first time it runs an affected action, with\nno Forge-side opt-in and nothing in your configuration mentioning it."
