  "contents": [{
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "**Who this is for:** anyone opening the Forge repository for the first\ntime and trying to work out where their change goes. &#x2A;*What you'll have at\nthe end:** the crate layering, the size of each piece, the directories that\nare not crates, and the half-dozen places where the first guess is wrong.\n&#x2A;*Time:** fifteen minutes."
  }, {
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "Forge is one Cargo workspace of twelve crates plus a root binary, and\nthe layering is strict enough that you can usually name the crate a change\nbelongs in before you open an editor. The exceptions are worth learning\nearly, because two of them put code in a crate whose name actively points\nsomewhere else."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-workspace-has-no-members-list",
    "content": "The root"
  }, {
    "heading": "the-workspace-has-no-members-list",
    "content": "declares `[workspace]` with only `exclude` and `resolver`. It has no\n`members` key. Membership is inferred from the path dependencies of the root\n`[package]`, which means **adding a crate to the workspace happens by\ndepending on it**, not by editing a list."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-workspace-has-no-members-list",
    "content": "Three directories are explicitly excluded and build on their own:\n`forge-config/generate-stores-config`, `forge-test/fuzz`, and\n`tools/generate-bazel-rc`."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-workspace-has-no-members-list",
    "content": "The version at the top of the root manifest is a `[package]` version, not\na `[workspace.package]` version. Nothing inherits it; every crate carries\nits own copy, which is why a release bump edits the version in fourteen\nfiles (seventeen once the two lock files and the changelog are counted).\nSee releases and versioning."
  }, {
