  }, {
    "heading": "the-layering",
    "content": "Every internal dependency points down this stack. It has no cycles, and\nthe shape is worth memorising because it tells you what a change can reach."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-layering",
    "content": "`forge-util` is the hub. Almost every trait that two crates need to\nagree on lives there rather than in the crate that looks like it owns the\nconcept: `Store` and `StoreDriver` are in `forge-util`, not\n`forge-store`, and the four scheduler state-manager traits are in\n`forge-util`, not `forge-scheduler`. This is deliberate: the\nimplementations depend on the traits, and the traits must not depend on the\nimplementations."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-layering",
    "content": "Its name says test utility; `forge-store` depends on it in\n`[dependencies]`, not `[dev-dependencies]`. Treat changes to it as changes\nto shipping code."
  }, {
    "heading": "where-the-first-guess-is-wrong",
    "content": "Six of these, and each one has cost somebody an afternoon."
  }, {
    "heading": "where-the-first-guess-is-wrong",
    "content": "**Worker bookkeeping lives in the scheduler.** `worker.rs`,\n`worker_registry.rs` and `api_worker_scheduler.rs` are in\n`forge-scheduler`. The scheduler's *model* of a worker (its\nproperties, its consumed resources, its liveness) belongs to the scheduler.\n`forge-worker` is only the runtime that executes actions."
  }, {
    "heading": "where-the-first-guess-is-wrong",
    "content": "**`forge-test/` contains only `fuzz/`.** The `#[forge_test]`\nattribute macro is in `forge-macro`. The directory name is a leftover."
  }, {
    "heading": "where-the-first-guess-is-wrong",
    "content": "**`forge-metric` does not depend on `forge-error`.** It cannot;\n`forge-error` depends on `forge-metric`, and the source carries a\ncomment explaining that the direction was chosen to break the cycle. A\nmetrics change that wants to return a `forge_error::Error` is a change\nthat needs rethinking."
  }, {
    "heading": "where-the-first-guess-is-wrong",
    "content": "**Generated proto code is checked in.** `forge-proto/genproto/` holds\ncommitted Rust, and the `[lib]` path points at it. You do not need `protoc`\nto build; you do need to regenerate and commit when a proto changes. See\nhow to extend."
  }, {
    "heading": "where-the-first-guess-is-wrong",
    "content": "**Store composition is not in one file.** A `verify` store wrapping a\n`fast_slow` over a `filesystem` is three files in `forge-store`, and\nthe thing that decides what wraps what is\n`default_store_factory.rs`. The store model\nexplains the semantics."
  }, {
    "heading": "where-the-first-guess-is-wrong",
    "content": "**Two metric systems coexist.** Which one you want depends on whether you\nare introspecting structure or graphing a number. See\ncodebase internals."
  }, {
    "heading": "directories-that-are-not-crates",
    "content": "Directory"
  }, {
    "heading": "directories-that-are-not-crates",
    "content": "What it is"
  }, {
    "heading": "directories-that-are-not-crates",
