    "heading": "directories-that-are-not-crates",
    "content": "`toolchain-examples/`, `templates/`"
  }, {
    "heading": "directories-that-are-not-crates",
    "content": "Starting points for downstream projects; both are `.bazelignore`d"
  }, {
    "heading": "directories-that-are-not-crates",
    "content": "`tools/`"
  }, {
    "heading": "directories-that-are-not-crates",
    "content": "Nix modules, pre-commit hooks, toolchain definitions, CI helpers"
  }, {
    "heading": "directories-that-are-not-crates",
    "content": "`web/`"
  }, {
    "heading": "directories-that-are-not-crates",
    "content": "The docs and marketing sites: Bun workspace, **not** part of the Bazel build"
  }, {
    "heading": "directories-that-are-not-crates",
    "content": "`assets/`"
  }, {
    "heading": "directories-that-are-not-crates",
    "content": "The logo SVGs"
  }, {
    "heading": "directories-that-are-not-crates",
    "content": "They are not alternative spellings of each other. `deploy/` is the\noverlays, `deployment-examples/` is copyable manifests, and `kubernetes/`\nis the building blocks the overlays compose."
  }, {
    "heading": "conventions-you-will-notice-immediately",
    "content": "Every manifest except the nested macro-derive crate's starts with\n`#:schema tools/cargo-with-detailed-deps.json`, which is what gives you\ncompletion and validation in a TOML-aware editor."
  }, {
    "heading": "conventions-you-will-notice-immediately",
    "content": "Every crate except `forge-proto` (generated code) and\n`forge-metric-macro-derive` has `lints.workspace = true` and no lint\nconfiguration of its own; all of it is centralised in the root\n`[workspace.lints]`."
  }, {
    "heading": "conventions-you-will-notice-immediately",
    "content": "Three license headers are in use. FSL-1.1-Apache-2.0 is the default and\ncovers the overwhelming majority of files; a handful are Apache-2.0; and two\nareas are **Business Source License**:\n`forge-util/src/metrics.rs` and all of\n`forge-worker/src/persistent_worker/`. Copy the header from the file\nnext to the one you are creating rather than from memory."
  }, {
    "heading": "common-questions",
    "content": "Two, plus a Bazel file: the spec goes in `forge-config`, the\nimplementation and its factory arm go in `forge-store`, and the new\nfile has to be added to `forge-store/BUILD.bazel`. The step-by-step\nis in how to extend."
  }, {
    "heading": "common-questions",
    "content": "Membership is derived from the root package's path dependencies. It\nworks, and it means the dependency graph and the workspace definition\ncannot drift apart, but it does mean a crate nothing depends on is\nsilently not in the workspace."
  }, {
    "heading": "common-questions",
    "content": "Yes. `cargo build --all` builds the whole workspace. CI runs Bazel as\nwell, and a few checks exist only there, so run `bazel test //...` before\nsubmitting. See the testing guide."
  }, {
    "heading": "common-questions",
    "content": "`src/bin/forge.rs`, in the root package. It builds the Tokio runtime\nby hand, constructs the stores, then assembles the gRPC routes. It is the\nsingle best file to read first if you want to see how the pieces connect."
  }, {
    "heading": "common-questions",
    "content": "The traits, the error model, the async rules and the two metric systems:\nthe conventions that a reviewer will expect you to already know."
  }],
