    "content": "Pool headroom, acquisitions that had to queue, and reconnects"
  }, {
    "heading": "which-metrics-exist",
    "content": "Three things worth knowing before you build a dashboard:"
  }, {
    "heading": "which-metrics-exist",
    "content": "`forge_cache_size` and `forge_cache_entries` are declared and\nnever emitted. The shipped\nrecording rules and the metrics README query both. Those rules have always\nreturned nothing."
  }, {
    "heading": "which-metrics-exist",
    "content": "Execution and worker fleet metrics come from the scheduler process only, and\nthey describe the fleet as that scheduler instance sees it. With several\nscheduler replicas, aggregate across instances before reading a fleet total."
  }, {
    "heading": "which-metrics-exist",
    "content": "The shipped recording rules and dashboard predate the worker, gRPC, scheduler,\nstore tier, health and connection pool families. Nothing under\n`deployment-examples/metrics/` queries them yet, so the queries below are the\nstarting point."
  }, {
    "heading": "queries-worth-having",
    "content": "Cache hit rate, per cache type:"
  }, {
    "heading": "queries-worth-having",
    "content": "How long actions wait before a worker picks them up, the number that tells you\nwhether to add workers:"
  }, {
    "heading": "queries-worth-having",
    "content": "Actions currently queued, which is the closest thing to a queue depth:"
  }, {
    "heading": "queries-worth-having",
    "content": "Success rate:"
  }, {
    "heading": "queries-worth-having",
    "content": "Actions the worker killed for memory, as a share of the sampled ones. The\nper-action resource histograms carry `execution_outcome` (`completed`,\n`killed_memory`, `killed_disk`), so a kill can be told from a completion and\nthe memory escalation rate read against it:"
  }, {
    "heading": "queries-worth-having",
    "content": "Workers connected to each scheduler instance, and how many of them are paused\nor draining:"
  }, {
    "heading": "queries-worth-having",
    "content": "Why workers are leaving, which separates a scaling event from a fleet that is\nbeing evicted for timeouts:"
  }, {
    "heading": "queries-worth-having",
    "content": "Matching pass latency, which is the scheduler's own cost per pass rather than\nhow long actions wait:"
  }, {
    "heading": "queries-worth-having",
    "content": "gRPC error rate per method, across every process:"
  }, {
    "heading": "queries-worth-having",
    "content": "Fast tier hit rate of a `fast_slow` store, which is what tells you whether the\nlocal disk in front of a bucket is earning its keep:"
  }, {
    "heading": "queries-worth-having",
    "content": "Peak memory per action at the 95th percentile, which is the number to size\nworker pods from (the scheduler records this sample with an empty\n`execution_instance`, so there is nothing useful to group by):"
  }, {
    "heading": "queries-worth-having",
    "content": "The repository ships 34 more as recording rules in\n`prometheus-recording-rules.yml`, grouped into `forge_execution`,\n`forge_cache`, `forge_performance` and `forge_slo`. Loading that\nfile gives you `forge:execution_queue_time_p95` and friends as\npre-computed series. The shipped dashboard does not query them; its panels\nread the raw `forge_execution_*` series directly."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-grafana-dashboard",
    "content": "A reference dashboard lives at\n.\nThe Compose stack provisions it automatically. Elsewhere: Dashboards → New →\nImport, paste the JSON, pick your Prometheus data source. It draws execution\nthroughput, success rate, active actions by stage and stage transitions from\n`forge_execution_*`; it has no cache, worker or gRPC panels."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-grafana-dashboard",
    "content": "If you add panels bound to `forge_cache_size` or\n`forge_cache_entries`, they will be empty forever. That is the metric,\nnot your pipeline."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-grafana-dashboard",
    "content": "`curl http://localhost:13133/health` returns healthy. The collector's\npipeline check is on, so this also fails when its exporters are failing."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-grafana-dashboard",
    "content": "`curl -s http://localhost:8888/metrics | grep otelcol_receiver_accepted_metric_points`\nis non-zero and climbing. If it is zero, Forge is not reaching the\ncollector."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-grafana-dashboard",
    "content": "`curl -s http://localhost:9090/metrics | grep forge_execution` shows\nseries on the collector's exporter, with the `forge_` prefix present."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-grafana-dashboard",
    "content": "In Prometheus at `http://localhost:9091`, `forge_execution_queue_time_bucket`\nreturns data after one build."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-grafana-dashboard",
    "content": "If the `forge_cache_*` series are missing but `forge_execution_*`\nare present, no store is wrapped in `cache_metrics`."
  }, {
