    "heading": "experimental_cloud_object_store",
    "content": "A generic blob store that will store files on the cloud\nprovider. This configuration will never delete files, so you are\nresponsible for purging old files in other ways.\nIt supports the following backends:"
  }, {
    "heading": "experimental_cloud_object_store",
    "content": "**Amazon S3:**\nS3 store will use Amazon's S3 service as a backend to store\nthe files. This configuration can be used to share files\nacross multiple instances. Uses system certificates for TLS\nverification via `rustls-platform-verifier`."
  }, {
    "heading": "experimental_cloud_object_store",
    "content": "**Example JSON5 config:**"
  }, {
    "heading": "experimental_cloud_object_store",
    "content": "**Google Cloud Storage:**\nGCS store uses Google's GCS service as a backend to store\nthe files. This configuration can be used to share files\nacross multiple instances."
  }, {
    "heading": "experimental_cloud_object_store",
    "content": "**Example JSON5 config:**"
  }, {
    "heading": "experimental_cloud_object_store",
    "content": "**Azure Blob Store:**\nAzure Blob store will use Microsoft's Azure Blob service as a\nbackend to store the files. This configuration can be used to\nshare files across multiple instances."
  }, {
    "heading": "experimental_cloud_object_store",
    "content": "**Example JSON5 config:**"
  }, {
    "heading": "experimental_cloud_object_store",
    "content": "**NetApp ONTAP S3:**\nNetApp ONTAP S3 store will use ONTAP's S3-compatible storage as a backend\nto store files. This store is specifically configured for ONTAP's S3 requirements\nincluding custom TLS configuration, credentials management, and proper vserver\nconfiguration."
  }, {
    "heading": "experimental_cloud_object_store",
    "content": "This store uses AWS environment variables for credentials:"
