    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "Field"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "Type"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "Required"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "Default"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "Description"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "`name`"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "string"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "\\{Index position in the workers list}"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "Name of the worker. This is give a more friendly name to a worker for logging and metric publishing. This is also the prefix of the worker id (i.e., \"\\{name}\\{uuidv6}\")."
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "`worker_api_endpoint`"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "EndpointConfig"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "Yes"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "Endpoint which the worker will connect to the scheduler's `WorkerApiService`."
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "`max_action_timeout`"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "integer (uint)"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "1200 (seconds / 20 minutes)"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "The maximum time an action is allowed to run. If a task requests for a timeout longer than this time limit, the task will be rejected. Value in seconds."
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "`max_upload_timeout`"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "integer (uint)"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "600 (seconds / 10 minutes)"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "Maximum time allowed for uploading action results to CAS after execution completes. If upload takes longer than this, the action fails with `DeadlineExceeded` and may be retried by the scheduler. Value in seconds."
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "`max_inflight_tasks`"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "integer (uint64)"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "0 (infinite tasks)"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "Maximum number of inflight tasks this worker can cope with."
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "`timeout_handled_externally`"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "boolean"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "false (`Forge` fully handles timeouts)"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "If timeout is handled in `entrypoint` or another wrapper script. If set to true `Forge` will not honor the timeout the action requested and instead will always force kill the action after `max_action_timeout` has been reached. If this is set to false, the smaller value of the action's timeout and `max_action_timeout` will be used to which `Forge` will kill the action."
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "`entrypoint`"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "string"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "\\{Use the command from the job request}"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "The command to execute on every execution request. This will be parsed as a command + arguments (not shell). Example: \"run.sh\" and a job with command: \"sleep 5\" will result in a command like: \"run.sh sleep 5\"."
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "`experimental_precondition_script`"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "string"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "An optional script to run before every action is processed on the worker. The value should be the full path to the script to execute and will pause all actions on the worker if it returns an exit code other than 0. If not set, then the worker will never pause and will continue to accept jobs according to the scheduler configuration. This is useful, for example, if the worker should not take any more actions until there is enough resource available on the machine to handle them."
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "`cas_fast_slow_store`"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "string"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "Yes"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "Underlying CAS store that the worker will use to download CAS artifacts. This store must be a `FastSlowStore`. The `fast` store must be a `FileSystemStore` because it will use hardlinks when building out the files instead of copying the files. The slow store must eventually resolve to the same store the scheduler/client uses to send job requests."
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "`upload_action_result`"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "UploadActionResultConfig"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "Configuration for uploading action results."
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "`work_directory`"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "string"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "Yes"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "The directory work jobs will be executed from. This directory will be fully managed by the worker service and will be purged on startup. This directory and the directory referenced in `local_filesystem_store_ref`'s `stores::FilesystemStore::content_path` must be on the same filesystem. Hardlinks will be used when placing files that are accessible to the jobs that are sourced from `local_filesystem_store_ref`'s `content_path`."
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "`platform_properties`"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "map of string to WorkerProperty"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "Yes"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "Properties of this worker. This configuration will be sent to the scheduler and used to tell the scheduler to restrict what should be executed on this worker."
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "`additional_environment`"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "map of string to EnvironmentSource"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "An optional mapping of environment names to set for the execution as well as those specified in the action itself. If set, will set each key as an environment variable before executing the job with the value of the environment variable being the value of the property of the action being executed of that name or the fixed value."
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "`directory_cache`"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "DirectoryCacheConfig"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "localworkerconfig",
    "content": "Optional directory cache configuration for improving performance by caching reconstructed input directories and using hardlinks instead of rebuilding them from CAS for every action."
  }, {
    "heading": "simplespec",
    "content": "Field"
  }, {
    "heading": "simplespec",
    "content": "Type"
  }, {
