    "heading": "evictionpolicy",
    "content": "Eviction policy always works on LRU (Least Recently Used). Any time an entry\nis touched it updates the timestamp. Inserts and updates will execute the\neviction policy removing any expired entries and/or the oldest entries\nuntil the store size becomes smaller than `max_bytes`."
  }, {
    "heading": "evictionpolicy",
    "content": "Field"
  }, {
    "heading": "evictionpolicy",
    "content": "Type"
  }, {
    "heading": "evictionpolicy",
    "content": "Required"
  }, {
    "heading": "evictionpolicy",
    "content": "Default"
  }, {
    "heading": "evictionpolicy",
    "content": "Description"
  }, {
    "heading": "evictionpolicy",
    "content": "`max_bytes`"
  }, {
    "heading": "evictionpolicy",
    "content": "integer (uint)"
  }, {
    "heading": "evictionpolicy",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "evictionpolicy",
    "content": "0"
  }, {
    "heading": "evictionpolicy",
    "content": "Maximum number of bytes before eviction takes place. Zero means never evict based on size."
  }, {
    "heading": "evictionpolicy",
    "content": "`evict_bytes`"
  }, {
    "heading": "evictionpolicy",
    "content": "integer (uint)"
  }, {
    "heading": "evictionpolicy",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "evictionpolicy",
    "content": "0"
  }, {
    "heading": "evictionpolicy",
    "content": "When eviction starts based on hitting `max_bytes`, continue until `max_bytes - evict_bytes` is met to create a low watermark. This stops operations from thrashing when the store is close to the limit."
  }, {
    "heading": "evictionpolicy",
    "content": "`max_seconds`"
  }, {
    "heading": "evictionpolicy",
    "content": "integer (uint32)"
  }, {
    "heading": "evictionpolicy",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "evictionpolicy",
    "content": "0"
  }, {
    "heading": "evictionpolicy",
    "content": "Maximum number of seconds for an entry to live since it was last accessed before it is evicted. Zero means never evict based on time."
  }, {
    "heading": "evictionpolicy",
    "content": "`max_count`"
  }, {
    "heading": "evictionpolicy",
    "content": "integer (uint64)"
  }, {
    "heading": "evictionpolicy",
    "content": "—"
  }, {
    "heading": "evictionpolicy",
    "content": "0"
  }, {
    "heading": "evictionpolicy",
    "content": "Maximum size of the store before an eviction takes place. Zero means never evict based on count."
  }, {
    "heading": "retry",
    "content": "Retry configuration. This configuration is exponential and each iteration\na jitter as a percentage is applied of the calculated delay. For example:"
  }, {
    "heading": "retry",
    "content": "will result in:"
  }, {
    "heading": "retry",
    "content": "Attempt"
  }, {
    "heading": "retry",
    "content": "Delay"
  }, {
    "heading": "retry",
    "content": "1"
  }, {
    "heading": "retry",
    "content": "0 ms"
  }, {
    "heading": "retry",
    "content": "2"
  }, {
    "heading": "retry",
    "content": "75 to 125 ms"
  }, {
    "heading": "retry",
    "content": "3"
  }, {
    "heading": "retry",
    "content": "150 to 250 ms"
  }, {
    "heading": "retry",
    "content": "4"
  }, {
    "heading": "retry",
    "content": "300 to 500 ms"
  }, {
    "heading": "retry",
    "content": "5"
  }, {
    "heading": "retry",
    "content": "600 ms to 1 s"
  }, {
    "heading": "retry",
    "content": "6"
  }, {
    "heading": "retry",
    "content": "1.2 to 2 s"
  }, {
    "heading": "retry",
    "content": "7"
  }, {
    "heading": "retry",
    "content": "2.4 to 4 s"
  }, {
    "heading": "retry",
    "content": "8"
  }, {
    "heading": "retry",
    "content": "4.8 to 8 s"
  }, {
    "heading": "retry",
    "content": "The total delay is additive, so this example produces 9.525 to 15.875 s of total delay for a single request."
  }, {
    "heading": "retry",
    "content": "Field"
  }, {
    "heading": "retry",
