  }, {
    "heading": "faq",
    "content": "`s3_backend_with_local_fast_cas.json5` for the store layer and the\n`docker-compose/` topology for the process split; that combination is the\nshape Production configuration describes at\nfull size. Don't start from `local_rbe_self_test.json5`; it's optimised for\nbeing readable in one screen, not for running a fleet."
  }, {
    "heading": "faq",
    "content": "Partly. Every file in `forge-config/examples/` is parsed by a unit test\n(`forge-config/tests/json5_test.rs`), so they all load. The\n`docker-compose/` deployment is what `run_integration_tests.sh` brings up,\nso it is exercised end to end in CI. `local_rbe_self_test.json5` is only\nparse-tested, and the backend-specific configs are not validated against\nlive cloud services, so treat credentials and endpoint syntax as the parts\nto double-check."
  }, {
    "heading": "faq",
    "content": "That's what pattern C is. `--strategy` and `--modify_execution_info` take\nmnemonic-scoped values, and `exec_properties` on a target routes it\nspecifically. The global flags are just defaults."
