    "heading": "run-a-build",
    "content": "The integration test checks for `SUCCESS Build` in the BuildStream output\nand checks that Forge did not log an error."
  }, {
    "heading": "troubleshooting",
    "content": "**BuildStream cannot connect.** Match the `http://localhost:50051`\nendpoint in `buildstream.conf` to the Forge listener. The local test\nuses an insecure HTTP URL."
  }, {
    "heading": "troubleshooting",
    "content": "**Uploads are missing.** Set `push: true` under `artifacts.servers` so\nBuildStream can write artifacts back to Forge."
  }, {
    "heading": "troubleshooting",
    "content": "**Remote actions do not match a worker.** Compare the platform properties\nBuildStream requests with the properties your Forge worker advertises.\nThe integration test worker advertises `ISA: x86-64`."
  }, {
    "heading": "faq",
    "content": "They configure different BuildStream subsystems: artifact push/pull\nstorage versus the execution, action-cache, and storage services used\nfor remote builds. Pointing every URL at the same Forge listener\nis fine; it exposes all of those services on one port."
  }, {
    "heading": "faq",
    "content": "BuildStream expresses these endpoints as URLs rather than bare\n`host:port` pairs. The checked-in integration test runs without TLS,\nhence `http://localhost:50051`."
  }, {
    "heading": "faq",
    "content": "BuildStream is pushing and pulling artifacts against one server. Next is making that server the team's."
  }],
