export let frontmatter = {
  "title": "Remote cache compression",
  "description": "Cut remote cache transfer bytes for compressible artifacts with REAPI zstd wire compression and Bazel's --remote_cache_compression."
};
export let structuredData = {
  "contents": [{
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "**Who this is for:** anyone whose clients reach Forge across a real\nnetwork and whose artifacts compress well. &#x2A;*What you'll have at the end:**\nzstd on the wire, with stores still holding raw bytes. &#x2A;*Time:** ten minutes."
  }, {
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "A config file you can edit (see Configuration), and a Bazel client you can pass flags to."
  }, {
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "Build artifacts are often highly compressible (object files, archives, test\nlogs), but a conventional remote cache transfers them byte-for-byte. With wire\ncompression, clients and server exchange blobs as zstd-compressed streams and\nonly the wire bytes shrink: Forge decompresses on upload and compresses on\ndownload at the gRPC boundary, so stores keep raw, uncompressed bytes and every\nexisting read path sees ordinary blobs."
  }, {
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "Forge implements the server side of the REAPI\n`compressed-blobs`\nextension with `zstd` as the only supported non-identity compressor, matching\nwhat Bazel's `--remote_cache_compression` flag speaks: ByteStream reads and\nwrites use `compressed-blobs/zstd/...` resource names, and the CAS batch RPCs\naccept and serve zstd-compressed payloads."
  }, {
    "heading": "requirements",
    "content": "A Bazel client with `--remote_cache_compression` (available since Bazel 5)."
  }, {
    "heading": "requirements",
    "content": "Wire compression is **optional and off until it is enabled somewhere in the\nForge process**. Without the configuration below or an explicitly\nenabled CAS `grpc` store, Forge does not advertise zstd, rejects\n`compressed-blobs/zstd` requests with `InvalidArgument`, and keeps its own\noutgoing transfers on the identity path, so clients fall back to identity\ntransfers."
  }, {
    "heading": "enabling-it",
    "content": "Set `remote_cache_compression: true` on the capabilities service for the\ninstance. The capabilities service advertises zstd to clients, and the\nByteStream and CAS services accept and serve compressed payloads for that\ninstance:"
  }, {
    "heading": "enabling-it",
    "content": "Then build with:"
  }, {
    "heading": "enabling-it",
    "content": "Clients only compress when the server advertises it, so enabling the option is\nsafe with a mixed fleet of clients: anything that doesn't request\n`compressed-blobs/zstd` keeps using identity transfers."
  }, {
    "heading": "enabling-it",
    "content": "See Servers and services for where the\ncapabilities service sits in the rest of the config."
  }, {
    "heading": "forge-to-forge-transfers",
    "content": "A `grpc` store with `store_type: \"cas\"` can compress its own uploads and\nfull-blob downloads to the upstream with `experimental_remote_cache_compression`.\nBlobs of 64 KiB and above go as `compressed-blobs/zstd`; smaller blobs and\nranged reads stay on the identity path. The upstream instance must have\n`remote_cache_compression` on its capabilities service, or compressed\nrequests fail with `InvalidArgument`."
  }, {
    "heading": "forge-to-forge-transfers",
    "content": "Enabling zstd on any capabilities instance or any CAS `grpc` store expresses\nprocess-wide intent. At config load, Forge then turns it on for every\nother CAS `grpc` store whose `experimental_remote_cache_compression` is\nomitted, so worker-to-CAS and proxy-to-upstream transfers pick it up without\nthe setting being repeated on each store. Declare the intent once and leave\nthe rest inherited:"
  }, {
    "heading": "forge-to-forge-transfers",
    "content": "To keep one link uncompressed (an older Forge, or a third-party cache\nwithout `compressed-blobs` support), set `experimental_remote_cache_compression:\nfalse` on that store. Forge logs a startup warning for a CAS `grpc` store\nthat opts out while zstd is enabled elsewhere, and a warning for\n`experimental_remote_cache_compression: true` on an `ac` store, where the\nsetting has no effect: `ac` stores are never eligible and never inherit."
  }, {
    "heading": "forge-to-forge-transfers",
    "content": "Compressed uploads from a `grpc` store do not resume mid-stream: a transport\nfailure part-way through surfaces to the caller, and outer retries re-send the\nwhole blob."
  }, {
    "heading": "semantics-worth-knowing",
    "content": "Resource names and digests always refer to the **uncompressed** blob; only\nthe bytes on the wire are compressed. ByteStream compressed writes report\n`committed_size` in compressed wire bytes, as the REAPI extension specifies."
  }, {
    "heading": "semantics-worth-knowing",
    "content": "Uploads are verified: Forge hashes the *decoded* bytes and rejects a\nblob whose decompressed content doesn't match the digest or size it was\naddressed with, bounding decompression by the expected size."
  }, {
    "heading": "semantics-worth-knowing",
    "content": "Batch reads fall back to identity when the zstd encoding would not be\nsmaller, so incompressible blobs don't pay the CPU and size overhead."
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-helps-and-when-it-doesnt",
    "content": "Compression pays off when clients reach the cache across a real network and the\nartifacts are compressible: uncompressed archives, binaries with debug info,\nand text-heavy outputs commonly shrink 2-10x on the wire. It does little on\nsame-rack links (the zstd CPU cost buys nothing when the wire isn't the\nbottleneck) and nothing for already-compressed artifacts."
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-helps-and-when-it-doesnt",
    "content": "Wire compression doesn't change what's stored: the CAS holds raw bytes. To also\nshrink bytes at rest, wrap the backing store in a `compression` store; see\nCompose stores. The two compose, since one\ncovers the wire and the other covers storage."
  }, {
    "heading": "steps",
    "content": "**Add `remote_cache_compression: true`** to the capabilities service for the\ninstance, and restart Forge."
  }, {
    "heading": "steps",
    "content": "**Run a build with `--remote_cache_compression`** against that instance."
  }, {
    "heading": "steps",
    "content": "**Compare transfer bytes** against the same build without the flag. If they\ndon't move, your artifacts weren't compressible."
  }, {
    "heading": "steps",
    "content": "The build succeeds with `--remote_cache_compression` and produces identical\noutputs to a build without it."
  }, {
    "heading": "steps",
    "content": "Bazel's reported remote cache transfer bytes drop for compressible targets."
  }, {
    "heading": "steps",
    "content": "Clients that don't pass the flag keep working against the same instance,\nunchanged."
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-doesnt-work",
    "content": "Forge only advertises zstd when `remote_cache_compression` is true on the\ncapabilities service **for that instance name**. An instance-name mismatch\nbetween the capabilities entry and the CAS or ByteStream entries is the usual\ncause."
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-doesnt-work",
    "content": "Your artifacts are already compressed, or the wire wasn't the bottleneck. Both\nare real answers; on a same-rack link there is nothing here to win."
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-doesnt-work",
    "content": "Yes. Clients only compress when the server advertises support, so anything that\ndoesn't request `compressed-blobs/zstd` keeps using identity transfers against\nthe same instance."
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-doesnt-work",
    "content": "Yes, but order matters at the store level: deduplication must operate on raw\ncontent, because identical chunks stop being identical after compression, so a `dedup`\nstore fed compressed bytes finds no duplicates. Wire compression is fine either\nway; it's undone at the gRPC boundary before any store sees the bytes."
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-doesnt-work",
    "content": "The other transfer-bytes lever: re-send only the parts of a large blob that\nchanged."
  }, {
    "heading": "when-it-doesnt-work",
    "content": "Shrinking bytes at rest instead of on the wire, with the `compression` store\nwrapper."
  }],
  "headings": [{
    "id": "requirements",
