  }, {
    "heading": "start-here-there-is-no-authentication",
    "content": "Open-source Forge authenticates no inbound request, on any service, in any\ndeployment. Not the CAS. Not the Action Cache. Not the Execution service. Not\nthe worker API. Not the admin endpoint. No bearer-token check, no API\nkey, no mTLS-identity-to-permission mapping; the code that would do it does\nnot exist in the tree."
  }, {
    "heading": "start-here-there-is-no-authentication",
    "content": "This is not a gap you close in the configuration file. The one server option\nthat looks like it might, `experimental_identity_header` with `required: true`,\nonly rejects requests that arrive without an OpenTelemetry `Baggage:\nenduser.id=...` header; the value is a telemetry label and is never checked\nagainst anything. &#x2A;*Your network is the authorization layer.** Everything below\nfollows from that one fact."
