    "heading": "the-committed-certificates-are-not-usable",
    "content": "The name is not a warning about best practice: the certificate expired, and\nits private key is public. Every client that talks to a listener using it must\npass `--insecure` or equivalent, which is what the repository's own TLS\nintegration test does. That is the only thing these files are for."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-committed-certificates-are-not-usable",
    "content": "No certificate-generation script exists anywhere in the tree. You supply real\nmaterial yourself, from whatever your organisation already uses: an internal CA,\ncert-manager in a cluster, or a public CA if the endpoint is genuinely public.\nTLS and auth walks through what the client side needs\nonce you have it."
  }, {
    "heading": "configure-tls",
    "content": "TLS is per-listener. Each server in the `servers` array carries its own\noptional `tls` block. Every field below is documented in\nthe configuration reference:"
  }, {
    "heading": "configure-tls",
